.C.TX. REAL PROPERTY RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    79→- P.R.T.C.TX. PLAT RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    80→- D.R.T.C.TX. DEED RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    81→- T. TRAFFIC SIGN\n    82→- G. GAS MARKER SIGN\n    83→- T. APPARENT GAS TEST STATION\n    84→\n    85→## Block 12: table — A table listing trees found on the property, providing an ID number, size (caliper in inches), and type (species) for each tree.\n    86→\n    87→TREE TABLE\n    88→| NO # | SIZ. | TYPE |\n    89→|---|---|---|\n    90→| 4000 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n    91→| 4001 | 15\" | HACKBERRY |\n    92→| 4002 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n    93→| 4003 | 12\" | LIVE OAK |\n    94→| 4004 | 22\" | LIVE OAK |\n    95→| 4006 | 13\" | LIVE OAK |\n    96→| 4007 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n    97→| 4008 | 13\" | HACKBERRY |\n    98→| 4009 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n    99→| 4010 | 18\" | CHINA BERRY |\n   100→| 4011 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1a6fb5a-883d-4cd9-82be-985a56b0d602","uuid":"74981093-1d68-4ded-9565-3e157b7c9403","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-04/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 4 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — This is a detailed site plan drawing showing an existing conditions survey. It includes property lines, buildings (existing slabs), trees, fences, utilities, and topographic contours. Key features include 'VALLEY VIEW ROAD' on the left side, 'LOT 2 MECEY SUBDIVISION' in the center, and 'LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS' on the right.\n\nThe drawing represents an existing conditions