4\n    21→\n    22→## Block 4: notes — List of cities where Bleyl Engineering operates.\n    23→\n    24→Austin Bryan Conroe Houston\n    25→\n    26→## Block 5: notes — Information regarding the coordinate system and bearing basis used for the survey.\n    27→\n    28→BEARING BASIS:\n    29→BEARINGS, DISTANCES AND COORDINATES ARE\n    30→BASED ON THE TEXAS COORDINATE SYSTEM\n    31→OF 1983 (NAD83) CENTRAL ZONE, GRID.\n    32→\n    33→## Block 6: notes — Indicates the job number associated with the survey document.\n    34→\n    35→JOB NUMBER: 20240953\n    36→\n    37→## Block 9: notes — A legend explaining the symbols and abbreviations used in the site plan drawing. It defines various symbols for pins, monuments, lines, and utility features.\n    38→\n    39→LEGEND\n    40→\n    41→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND UNLESS NOTED\n    42→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN SET W/CAP MARKED S.L.S. RPLS 518\n    43→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED CARTER BURGESS\n    44→- 1/2\" STEEL PIN FOUND W/CAP MARKED LIND & ASSOC.\n    45→- MAG NAIL SET\n    46→- 3/4\" BRASS MONUMENT FOUND\n    47→- NAIL FOUND\n    48→- 60D NAIL FOUND\n    49→- CHAIN LINK FENCE\n    50→- IRON PIPE FOUND\n    51→- MAG NAIL FOUND\n    52→- \"X\" FOUND IN CONCRETE\n    53→- WATER METER\n    54→- WATER VALVE\n    55→- SPRINKLE FOUND\n    56→- WOOD FENCE\n    57→- UTILITY POLE\n    58→- WIRE FENCE\n    59→- LIGHT POLE\n    60→- CRETE FENCE\n    61→- PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT\n    62→- ELECTRIC EASEMENT\n    63→- WATER, WASTEWATER EASEMENT\n    64→- P.U.E. D.U.E. DRAINAGE EASEMENT\n    65→- W.W.L.E. WASTEWATER LINE\n    66→- W.L. WATER LINE\n    67→- O.H.U.L. OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\n    68→- T.L. TOWN LOT\n    69→- C.I. CURB INLET\n    70→- (BRG-DIST) RECORD CALL ADJOINER\n    71→- - DECIDUOUS TREE (VARIOUS TYPES)\n    72→- - CLEAN-OUT\n    73→- - FIRE HYDRANT\n    74→- - AIR CONDITIONER\n    75→- - SIGN POST\n    76→- - TRANSFORMER ON PAD\n    77→- O.P.R.T.C.TX. OFFICIAL PUBLIC RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    78→- R.P.R.T.C.TX. REAL PROPERTY RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    79→- P.R.T.C.TX. PLAT RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    80→- D.R.T.C.TX. DEED RECORDS OF TRAVIS COUNTY, TEXAS\n    81→- T. TRAFFIC SIGN\n    82→- G. GAS MARKER SIGN\n    83→- T. APPARENT GAS TEST STATION\n    84→\n    85→## Block 12: table — A table listing trees found on the property, providing an ID number, size (caliper in inches), and type (species) for each tree.\n    86→\n    87→TREE TABLE\n    88→| NO # | SIZ. | TYPE |\n    89→|---|---|---|\n    90→| 4000 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n    91→| 4001 | 15\" | HACKBERRY |\n    92→| 4002 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n    93→| 4003 | 12\" | LIVE OAK |\n    94→| 4004 | 22\" | LIVE OAK |\n    95→| 4006 | 13\" | LIVE OAK |\n    96→| 4007 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n    97→| 4008 | 13\" | HACKBERRY |\n    98→| 4009 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n    99→| 4010 | 18\" | CHINA BERRY |\n   100→| 4011 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n   101→| 4012 | 12\" | HACKBERRY |\n   102→| 4013 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n   103→| 4014 | 9\" | HACKBERRY |\n   104→| 4015 | 8\" | HACKBERRY |\n   105→| 4016 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n   106→| 4017 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n   107→| 4019 | 10\" | LIVE OAK |\n   108→| 4022 | 24\" | PECAN |\n   109→| 4023 | 24\" | M |\n   110→| 4024 | 8\" | ELM |\n   111→| 4025 | 28\" | LIVE OAK |\n   112→| 4026 | 28\" | HACKBERRY |\n   113→| 4027 | 15\" | M |\n   114→| 4028 | 36\" | HACKBERRY |\n   115→| 4030 | 14\" | PECAN |\n   116→| 4031 | 16\" | LIVE OAK |\n   117→| 4032 | 18\" | LIVE OAK |\n   118→| 4033 | 11\" | ELM |\n   119→| 4034 | 20\" | CHINA BERRY |\n   120→| 4035 | 16\" | ELM |\n   121→| 4036 | 14\" | PECAN |\n   122→| 4037 | 11\" | ASH |\n   123→| 4038 | 20\" | HACKBERRY |\n   124→| 4040 | 11\" | HACKBERRY |\n   125→| 4041 | 13\" | ELM |\n   126→| 4042 | 34\" | LIVE OAK |\n   127→| 4043 | 15\" | LIVE OAK |\n   128→| 4044 | 14\" | LIVE OAK |\n   129→| 4045 | 20\" | LIVE OAK |\n   130→| 4046 | 17\" | LIVE OAK |\n   131→| 4047 | 16\" | PINE |\n   132→\n   133→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you re