{"level":30,"time":1776457984777,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31) and provide the following:\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Lines**: Where are the overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this sheet? Describe their locations and routing (e.g., \"along Valley View Road,\" \"through the southeast portion,\" etc.). Are conductor locations marked or dimensioned?\n\n2. **Tree Locations**: Identify the locations of proposed trees on the landscape plan. Which trees (by symbol or location description) are positioned nearest to the overhead electric lines? List any trees within apparent proximity (visual estimate within 25-30 feet) to the OHE lines.\n\n3. **Tree Symbols & Types**: The blocks describe trees as SY (Street Yard), PL (Parking Lot), P (Parking Buffer), and M (Mitigation). Which symbol types are located near the overhead electric lines?\n\n4. **Clearance Appearance**: Based on visual inspection, do the proposed trees appear to be at safe distances from the overhead electric conductors? Are any trees positioned directly under or very close to the OHE lines?\n\n5. **Documentation**: Are there any dimensions, notes, or callouts on the sheet that specifically address tree clearances from the overhead electric lines?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided image of the landscape plan (which is labeled as **Sheet 28 of 35**, rather than Sheet 31 as noted in the prompt), here is the visual analysis regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Overhead Electric Lines**\n*   **Location & Routing:** Overhead electric lines are indicated by a dashed line with the text label \"-OHE-\". This line runs horizontally along the entire bottom (southern) boundary of the site plan shown on this sheet.\n*   **Conductor Locations:** There are no specific marks, symbols, or dimensions indicating exact individual conductor locations along this routing line on this sheet.\n\n**2. Tree Locations**\n*   **Proposed Trees Near OHE:** There is a row of proposed trees located along the southern edge of the property, positioned just north of the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **Proximity:** Based on the graphical scale provided in the bottom right corner (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), the centers of these trees appear to be visually estimated at approximately 10 to 15 feet from the \"-OHE-\" line.\n\n**3. Tree Symbols & Types**\n*   The tree symbols located nearest to the southern overhead electric line are circles containing the letter **\"M\"**.\n*   According to the text block below the \"KEY NOTES\" section on the right side of the page, **\"M\"** stands for **\"MITIGATION TREE\"**. There are at least four distinct trees labeled \"M\" positioned along this southern boundary near the OHE line. I do not see \"SY\", \"PL\", or \"P\" labeled trees directly adjacent to this specific OHE line.\n\n**4. Clearance Appearance**\n*   Based strictly on visual inspection of the plan, the proposed \"M\" (Mitigation) trees appear to be positioned very close to the OHE lines.\n*   While their centers do not appear to be directly underneath the line, the larger circles representing their potential canopies are drawn overlapping or nearly touching the dashed \"-OHE-\" line. At the 1\"=20' scale, a 10-15 foot distance to the trunk may pose clearance issues depending on the mature canopy spread of the specific mitigation tree species chosen.\n\n**5. Documentation**\n*   There are **no** dimensions, specific callouts, or notes on this sheet that explicitly address required tree clearances or safe distances from the overhead electric lines. Neither the \"IRRIGATION NOTES\", the general \"NOTE\" section, nor the \"KEY NOTES\" mention electric utilities or clearances.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1563,"outputTo