{"level":30,"time":1776457987203,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and identify: 1) All transformer pad locations on the site - provide their specific locations relative to buildings and other features; 2) Any dimensions or clearance measurements shown between transformer pads and adjacent buildings, structures, fences, or other site features; 3) The orientation and location of transformer access doors; 4) Any notes or specifications about transformer sizing or specifications; 5) The proximity of transformer pads to parking areas, driveways, or vehicle circulation areas. Provide a detailed spatial description of each transformer's location and any clearances that are labeled or dimensioned on the drawing.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21), here is a detailed analysis of the electrical transformer pads as requested:\n\n**1) Transformer Pad Locations**\nThere are five distinct transformer pads identified on the site plan, all labeled with the exact text \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\". They are spatially located as follows:\n*   **Transformer Pad 1 (Northwest):** Located on the west side of the site, specifically west of **Bldg. 1** and north of the circular paved turnaround area. It is situated in the landscaped/green space area near the main entrance drive.\n*   **Transformer Pad 2 (West-Central):** Located along the western edge of the site, directly west of **Bldg. 2** (near Unit 201). It is positioned between the building's front parking/drive aisle and the western property line/sidewalk easement.\n*   **Transformer Pad 3 (Southwest):** Located near the southwest corner of the site, directly west of **Bldg. 8** (near Unit 801). Similar to Pad 2, it sits between the drive aisle and the western boundary.\n*   **Transformer Pad 4 (East-Central):** Located in the east-central portion of the site, situated between the east side of **Bldg. 4** (near Unit 404) and the west side of **Bldg. 5**. It is positioned on a landscaped corner where the internal drive aisles intersect.\n*   **Transformer Pad 5 (Southeast):** Located in the southeastern portion of the site, situated between the east side of **Bldg. 7** and the west side of **Bldg. 6** (near Units 602 and 603). It sits within a landscaped island that separates the parking areas of the two buildings.\n\n**2) Dimensions or Clearance Measurements**\n*   **None are shown.** There are absolutely no dimension lines, setback measurements, or clearance distances explicitly labeled on this drawing between any of the transformer pads and adjacent buildings, structures, fences, or property lines. \n\n**3) Orientation and Location of Transformer Access Doors**\n*   **Not indicated.** The transformer pads are depicted schematically as simple square outlines (some containing a smaller circle symbol) connected to the blue electrical routing lines. There are no markings, arrows, or \"clear workspace\" hatches indicating the orientation of access doors or which side must remain unobstructed.\n\n**4) Notes or Specifications about Transformer Sizing**\n*   **None are provided.** The pads are exclusively labeled with the generic callout \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\". There is no text indicating kVA sizing, voltage, specific equipment models, or utility provider specifications next to the pads.\n*   The \"**Utility Notes**\" section in the bottom right corner contains four notes regarding verifying existing utilities and specifications for private domestic water and wastewater branches, but mentions nothing regarding electrical transformers.\n\n**5) Proximity to Parking Areas, Driveways, or Vehicle Circulation**\n*   All five transformer pads are located in immediate proximity to internal vehicle circulation areas:\n    *   **Pad 1** is adjacent to the main entrance driveway and the curved curb of the turnaround.\n    *   **Pads 2 and 3** are located directly adjacent to the curb of the westernmost drive aisle and parallel parking spaces, separated only by a narrow strip of landscaping/curb.\n    *   **Pad 4** is situated on the corner of a landscaped peninsula directly abutting a T-intersection of the internal drive aisles.\n    *   **Pad 5** is located within a landscaped median/island that is closely bounded on three sides by drive aisles and perpendicular parking spaces serving Buildings 6 and 7.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1443,"outputTokens":790,"totalTokens":4402,"reasoningTokens":2169},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not