ot indicated.** The transformer pads are depicted schematically as simple square outlines (some containing a smaller circle symbol) connected to the blue electrical routing lines. There are no markings, arrows, or \"clear workspace\" hatches indicating the orientation of access doors or which side must remain unobstructed.\n\n**4) Notes or Specifications about Transformer Sizing**\n*   **None are provided.** The pads are exclusively labeled with the generic callout \"**Electrical Transformer Pad**\". There is no text indicating kVA sizing, voltage, specific equipment models, or utility provider specifications next to the pads.\n*   The \"**Utility Notes**\" section in the bottom right corner contains four notes regarding verifying existing utilities and specifications for private domestic water and wastewater branches, but mentions nothing regarding electrical transformers.\n\n**5) Proximity to Parking Areas, Driveways, or Vehicle Circulation**\n*   All five transformer pads are located in immediate proximity to internal vehicle circulation areas:\n    *   **Pad 1** is adjacent to the main entrance driveway and the curved curb of the turnaround.\n    *   **Pads 2 and 3** are located directly adjacent to the curb of the westernmost drive aisle and parallel parking spaces, separated only by a narrow strip of landscaping/curb.\n    *   **Pad 4** is situated on the corner of a landscaped peninsula directly abutting a T-intersection of the internal drive aisles.\n    *   **Pad 5** is located within a landscaped median/island that is closely bounded on three sides by drive aisles and perpendicular parking spaces serving Buildings 6 and 7.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1443,"outputTokens":790,"totalTokens":4402,"reasoningTokens":2169},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"