{"level":30,"time":1776458004621,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: 1) All overhead electric utility lines shown on the plan, including their paths across the site. 2) The locations of electric poles or transmission structures. 3) All tree symbols and their locations relative to overhead electric lines and poles. 4) What trees are proposed to be planted and where. Provide the specific locations and distances from electric infrastructure where possible.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the analysis of the requested elements:\n\n**1) Overhead Electric Utility Lines**\n*   A single overhead electric line is identified by a line designated with the text \"**-OHE-**\".\n*   **Path:** It runs horizontally across the entire bottom (southern) boundary of the site plan. It is located just inside the property limits, running parallel to the Limits of Construction (\"-LOC-\") line.\n\n**2) Electric Poles or Transmission Structures**\n*   Electric poles are indicated by small circular symbols with an \"x\" or cross inside them, placed directly on the \"-OHE-\" line.\n*   **Locations:** There are three visible pole symbols along this path:\n    *   One near the bottom-left corner of the site plan area.\n    *   One roughly in the lower-middle section of the site line.\n    *   One near the bottom-right corner of the site line.\n\n**3) Tree Symbols and Their Locations Relative to Lines/Poles**\n*   There is a linear row of six tree symbols placed along the bottom boundary of the site.\n*   **Relative Location:** The \"-OHE-\" utility line passes directly through the canopy symbols of all six of these trees. For the majority of these trees, the overhead electric line is depicted running straight through or extremely close to the center point (trunk) of the tree symbol.\n*   The electric pole symbols are similarly located right beside or within the canopy footprints of these trees.\n\n**4) Proposed Trees and Specific Locations/Distances**\n*   The trees planted along this bottom boundary have a distinct \"**M**\" labeled inside their center circles.\n*   According to the \"KEY NOTES\" legend on the right side of the document, \"**M**\" stands for \"**M - MITIGATION TREE**\".\n*   **Specific Locations:** These Mitigation Trees are proposed in a row along the bottom edge of the property, directly under the path of the overhead electric line.\n*   **Distances:** There are **no numerical distances or dimension lines** provided on this plan to indicate the exact spacing or clearance between the proposed mitigation trees and the overhead electric line or poles. Visually, the plan shows the trees planted directly underneath the utility line with zero horizontal clearance shown from the trunks.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1393,"outputTokens":494,"totalTokens":4845,"reasoningTokens":2958},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you 