{"level":30,"time":1776458012181,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Identify and document all overhead electric utility facilities on this existing conditions survey. Specifically:\n1. Locate all utility poles marked with the \"UTILITY POLE\" symbol\n2. Identify overhead utility lines (marked \"O.H.U.L.\") and their routing across the property\n3. Note the specific locations of poles and lines relative to property boundaries and the proposed building footprint areas\n4. Identify any down guy wires or guy anchors (support cables from poles to ground anchors)\n5. Describe the voltage class if labeled (distribution vs transmission)\n6. Note easement designations related to electric facilities\n\nProvide specific spatial descriptions (north/south/east/west) and approximate locations relative to the labeled lot and road.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided boundary, topographic, and tree survey for Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision, here is the documentation of the overhead electric utility facilities visible on the plan:\n\n**1 & 2. Utility Poles and Overhead Utility Lines (O.H.U.L.) Routing**\nThe survey identifies a network of overhead utility lines (dashed lines labeled \"O.H.U.L.\") and utility poles (circle symbol with a cross) primarily located along the western and northern edges of the property.\n*   **Western Boundary (Along Valley View Road):** An overhead utility line runs generally north-to-south, roughly parallel to the western property line adjacent to Valley View Road. There are three distinct utility poles along this route:\n    *   One pole is located near the southwest corner of the property, situated just inside the property line.\n    *   A second pole is located approximately midway along the western property boundary.\n    *   A third pole is situated near the northwest corner of the property.\n*   **Northern Crossing:** From the utility pole near the northwest corner, the overhead utility line routes eastward, crossing the northern portion of the property.\n    *   It spans across an area proposed for \"ASPHALT\" and \"CONC.\" (driveway/access areas).\n    *   This line connects to a fourth utility pole located on the northern property boundary line (the line labeled \"S83°08'28\"E 419.86'\").\n    *   From this northern pole, the line appears to continue eastward, off the surveyed area.\n\n**3. Locations Relative to Property Boundaries and Proposed Building Footprint**\n*   **Relative to Boundaries:** The primary O.H.U.L. run closely follows the western property boundary line. A secondary run cuts diagonally across the northwest corner to intersect the northern property boundary line.\n*   **Relative to Building Footprint:** The overhead lines do not appear to route directly over the main proposed building structure (indicated by the large central footprint areas labeled \"SLAB\"). However, the O.H.U.L. that crosses from the northwest corner to the northern boundary routes directly over proposed paved surfaces (labeled \"ASPHALT\" and \"CONC.\") that serve as access drives or parking areas on the north side of the main building.\n\n**4. Down Guy Wires or Guy Anchors**\n*   There is one visible down guy wire and anchor associated with the utility pole located on the **northern property boundary**. A dashed line extends southward from this pole into the property, terminating in a guy anchor symbol (a small circle with a line through it). This anchor is situated within an area heavily populated with trees, just north of the proposed concrete/asphalt drive.\n\n**5. Voltage Class**\n*   The voltage class (e.g., distribution or transmission voltages like 12kV, 138kV) is **not labeled** or indicated anywhere on this existing conditions survey. The lines are simply designated generically as \"O.H.U.L.\" (Overhead Utility Line).\n\n**6. Easement Designations Related to Electric Facilities**\nThe survey designates several easements pertaining to electrical utilities. I have transcribed them exactly as they appear on the plan:\n*   **Northern Boundary:** Along the northern property line, where one of the utility poles is located, there is a designated easement labeled exactly as: **\"5' ELEC., TELE. & C.A.T.V. EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX\"**\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Along the southern property line, there is a designated easement labeled exactly as: **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 76, PG. 18 P.R.T.C.TX\"** (Note: No overhead lines or poles are shown within this specific southern easement on this drawing).\n*   Also on the southern boundary is a broader utility easement labeled: **\"5' PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX\"**","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1458,"outputTokens":869,"totalTokens":5629,"reasoningTokens":3302},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Identify and document all overhead electric utility facilities on this existing conditions survey. Specifically:\n1. Locate all utility poles marked with the \"UTILITY POLE\" symbol\n2. Identify overhead utility lines (marked \"O.H.U.L.\") and their routing across the property\n3. Note the specific locations of poles and lines relative to property boundaries and the proposed building footprint areas\n4. Identify any down guy wires or guy anchors (support cables from poles to ground anchors)\n5. Describe the voltage class if labeled (distribution vs transmission)\n6. Note easement designations related to electric facilities\n\nProvide specific spatial descriptions (north/south/east/west) and approximate locations relative to the labeled lot and road."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-gWuZIrengk7MgahFzeN08Uxc","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 17 Apr 2026 20:33:32 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"cle1::cle1::pm82d-1776457952536-92a2067cb317"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided boundary, topographic, and tree survey for Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision, here is the documentation of the overhead electric utility facilities visible on the plan:\n\n**1 & 2. Utility Poles and Overhead Utility Lines (O.H.U.L.) Routing**\nThe survey identifies a network of overhead utility lines (dashed lines labeled \"O.H.U.L.\") and utility poles (circle symbol with a cross) primarily located along the western and northern edges of the property.\n*   **Western Boundary (Along Valley View Road):** An overhead utility line runs generally north-to-south, roughly parallel to the western property line adjacent to Valley View Road. There are three distinct utility poles along this route:\n    *   One pole is located near the southwest corner of the property, situated just inside the property line.\n    *   A second pole is located approximately midway along the western property boundary.\n    *   A third pole is situated near the northwest corner of the property.\n*   **Northern Crossing:** From the utility pole near the northwest corner, the overhead utility line routes eastward, crossing the northern portion of the property.\n    *   It spans across an area proposed for \"ASPHALT\" and \"CONC.\" (driveway/access areas).\n    *   This line connects to a fourth utility pole located on the northern property boundary line (the line labeled \"S83°08'28\"E 419.86'\").\n    *   From this northern pole, the line appears to continue eastward, off the surveyed area.\n\n**3. Locations Relative to Property Boundaries and Proposed Building Footprint**\n*   **Relative to Boundaries:** The primary O.H.U.L. run closely follows the western property boundary line. A secondary run cuts diagonally across the northwest corner to intersect the northern property boundary line.\n*   **Relative to Building Footprint:** The overhead lines do not appear to route directly over the main proposed building structure (indicated by the large central footprint areas labeled \"SLAB\"). However, the O.H.U.L. that crosses from the northwest corner to the northern boundary routes directly over proposed paved surfaces (labeled \"ASPHALT\" and \"CONC.\") that serve as access drives or parking areas on the north side of the main building.\n\n**4. Down Guy Wires or Guy Anchors**\n*   There is one visible down guy wire and anchor associated with the utility pole located on the **northern property boundary**. A dashed line extends southward from this pole into the property, terminating in a guy anchor symbol (a small circle with a line through it). This anchor is situated within an area heavily populated with trees, just north of the proposed concrete/asphalt drive.\n\n**5. Voltage Class**\n*   The voltage class (e.g., distribution or transmission voltages like 12kV, 138kV) is **not labeled** or indicated anywhere on this existing conditions survey. The lines are simply designated generically as \"O.H.U.L.\" (Overhead Utility Line).\n\n**6. Easement Designations Related to Electric Facilities**\nThe survey designates several easements pertaining to electrical utilities. I have transcribed them exactly as they appear on the plan:\n*   **Northern Boundary:** Along the northern property line, where one of the utility poles is located, there is a designated easement labeled exactly as: **\"5' ELEC., TELE. & C.A.T.V. EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX\"**\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Along the southern property line, there is a designated easement labeled exactly as: **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT VOL. 76, PG. 18 P.R.T.C.TX\"** (Note: No overhead lines or poles are shown within this specific southern easement on this drawing).\n*   Also on the southern boundary is a broader utility easement labeled: **\"5' PUBLIC UTILITY EASEMENT VOL. 84, PG. 13 P.R.T.C.TX\"**","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1458,"outputTokens":869,"totalTokens":5629,"reasoningTokens":3302},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":1336378.862907,"endTime":1395376.681141,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"4ZjiaZzmFdKCueUPqMS8uAw"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.052968","marketCost":"0.052968","inferenceCost":"0.052968","inputInferenceCost":"0.002916","outputInferenceCost":"0.050052","generationId":"gen_01KPEJABV0M0EFXQP07NHY3QR8"}}},"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided boundary, topographic, and tree survey for Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision, here is the documentation of the overhead electric utility facilities visible on the plan:\n\n**1 & 2. Utility Poles and Overhead Utility Lines (O.H.U.L.) Routing**\nThe survey identifies a network of overhead utility lines (dashed lines labeled \"O.H.U.L.\") and utility poles (circle symbol with a cross) primarily located along the western and northern edges of the property.\n*   *