{"level":30,"time":1776458025681,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Focus on the Landscape Plan and identify the tree mitigation planting:\n\n1. **Mitigation Trees (M) Species**: Using the plant legend/schedule from Sheet 35, which tree species are shown as mitigation trees (marked \"M\") on this landscape plan? Look at the tree symbols and determine if they correspond to:\n   - Cedar Elm\n   - Live Oak\n   - Texas Mountain Laurel\n   - Mexican Redbud\n   \n   Based on the symbols used (different circles for different species as shown in Block 17 of Sheet 35), which symbols appear on the landscape plan as mitigation trees near the OHE line?\n\n2. **Specific Locations**: Are the \"M\" trees near the southern OHE line specifically Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, or Mexican Redbud? \n\n3. **Plant Symbol Guide**: Describe any symbols or notations visible that indicate tree species on this sheet. Do the tree symbols use the same symbols as shown in the plant list (e.g., circles with different patterns)?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is the information regarding the tree mitigation planting:\n\n**Important Note:** The provided image is only Sheet 28. It does not include the plant legend/schedule from Sheet 35. Therefore, while I can identify the symbols and labels on this plan, I cannot definitively match them to specific species names (like Cedar Elm, Live Oak, etc.) without that corresponding legend.\n\nHere is what is explicitly visible on the plan:\n\n**1 & 2. Mitigation Trees (M) and Specific Locations near the OHE Line:**\n*   Locating the southern boundary marked with the dashed line labeled **\"- - - OHE - - -\"**, there are trees positioned just above this line (towards the bottom right of the site plan).\n*   There are trees in this specific area accompanied by the label **\"M\"**. \n*   According to the **KEY NOTES** section on the right side of the sheet, **\"M\"** stands for **\"M - MITIGATION TREE\"**.\n*   The specific graphic symbol used for the mitigation trees near the southern OHE line is a **circle with a simple plus sign (\"+\") inside**. \n*   Because the plant schedule is not on this sheet, I cannot confirm if the \"circle with a +\" symbol corresponds to Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, or Mexican Redbud.\n\n**3. Plant Symbol Guide:**\n*   There is no plant symbol schedule or legend on this specific sheet that defines the tree species. \n*   However, the plan clearly uses different symbols to differentiate tree species. Visible tree symbols on this sheet include:\n    *   **Circle with a plus (\"+\") inside:** Found near the southern OHE line and the eastern boundary, some labeled \"M\".\n    *   **Circle with a central dot/small inner circle:** Found along the northern boundary, some labeled \"M\".\n    *   **Circle with a cross and an inner circle (wheel-like):** Found along the western boundary (Street Yard), labeled \"SY/M\".\n*   The **KEY NOTES** provide functional labels rather than species names:\n    *   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE...\n    *   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE...\n    *   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n    *   **M** - MITIGATION TREE","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1525,"outputTokens":508,"totalTokens":3955,"reasoningTokens":1922},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, charac