{"level":30,"time":1776458027008,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"This is the landscape plan showing proposed plantings. I need to identify: 1) All tree locations (mark them as individual symbols on the drawing), 2) Whether trees appear to be located near any utility lines or infrastructure shown on the plan (overhead electric OHE lines, underground electric lines). 3) Describe the specific locations of any trees that appear to be within visible utility easement areas or close to underground electric lines shown. 4) Note any trees that appear in street yard areas versus parking lots versus common open space. Provide spatial references using building locations or compass directions (north, south, east, west, northeast, etc.).","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here is an analysis addressing your specific questions regarding tree locations, utility conflicts, and tree categorization.\n\n### 1. General Tree Locations and Identification Key\nTrees are denoted on the plan as large circular symbols, typically with a crosshair or a smaller circle in the center. The plan uses specific letter codes next to these symbols to categorize them, as defined in the \"KEY NOTES\" on the right side:\n*   **SY** - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **PL** - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\n*   **P** - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\n*   **M** - MITIGATION TREE\n\n**Overall Locations:** The majority of the proposed trees are located along the perimeter of the property boundaries (North, South, East, and West). There are also a few located within parking lot islands and smaller ornamental trees within the central building courtyard.\n\n### 2 & 3. Utility Lines and Potential Tree Conflicts\nThere are visible instances where proposed trees appear to be located directly over or very close to depicted utility lines.\n\n*   **South Property Boundary (Overhead Electric Conflict):**\n    *   There is a line running east-west along the entire southern property boundary labeled precisely as **\"- OHE -\"** (Overhead Electric).\n    *   There are five (5) large trees explicitly labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree) planted in a row directly along this southern boundary. The \"- OHE -\" line passes directly through the center of these tree symbols, indicating they are proposed to be planted directly underneath the overhead power lines.\n\n*   **West Property Boundary / Street Yard (Underground Electric Conflict):**\n    *   Along the western edge of the site, adjacent to \"Valley View Road,\" there is an underground utility line running north-south labeled **\"- E -\"**.\n    *   This area contains a shaded zone designated by Key Note **\"H-2\"** (\"STREET YARD\").\n    *   Within this Street Yard area, there are three (3) large trees labeled **\"SY/M\"**. These trees are positioned extremely close to or directly overlapping the \"- E -\" (electric) and \"- W -\" (water) utility lines running parallel to the street.\n\n### 4. Tree Categorization by Area (Street Yard vs. Parking Lot vs. Common Open Space)\n\nUsing spatial references and the provided plan keys, the trees are categorized as follows:\n\n*   **Street Yard Areas:**\n    *   **Location:** The entire western frontage facing Valley View Road. This area is designated with a gray shading pattern corresponding to Key Note **\"H-2\"** (\"STREET YARD\").\n    *   **Trees:** The trees in this specific area are labeled **\"SY/M\"**, indicating they serve as both Street Yard Trees and Mitigation Trees.\n\n*   **Parking Lots:**\n    *   **Location:** Interior paved areas on the north, west, and east sides of the main building footprint.\n    *   **Trees:**\n        *   There is a tree specifically labeled **\"PL\"** (Parking Lot Tree) located within a landscape island in the northwest parking area.\n        *   There are trees labeled **\"P\"** (Parking Buffer Point Tree) located around the perimeter of the eastern parking area, separating the parking from the property line.\n\n*   **Mitigation / Perimeter Buffer:**\n    *   **Location:** The North, East, and South property lines.\n    *   **Trees:** These boundary areas are predominantly planted with trees labeled **\"M\"** (Mitigation Tree) to serve as a perimeter buffer. A row of six \"M\" trees lines the northern boundary, several \"M\" trees surround the \"FILTRATION BASIN\" in the northeast, and five \"M\" trees line the southern boundary.\n\n*   **Common Open Space:**\n    *   While Key Note **\"H-5\"** denotes \"PRIVATE COMMON OPEN SPACE,\" there are no large, explicitly labeled SY, PL, P, or M trees within the central courtyard between the building wings. The central courtyard features paved walkways and smaller circular symbols that likely represent smaller, unspecified ornamental plantings or shrubs not categorized by the main mitigation/yard key.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1440,"outputTokens":919,"totalTokens":5249,"reasoningTokens":2890},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be pre