ocated further down the left side of the drawing (further West along the Northern boundary), near the callout `N27°29'58\"E 96.10'`.\n\n**2. Overhead Utility Lines/Conductors Running Across the Property**\n*   **Yes, there is an overhead line routing across the site.**\n*   A line branches off from the power pole located near the top-left (North-East corner) of the property. \n*   This line crosses over the front yard/driveway area, routing downwards and to the right on the page (South-West direction). \n*   It terminates at a symbol on the existing building slab labeled **\"ELEC. METER\"**.\n\n**3. Utility Lines Marked as O.H.U.L.**\n*   The lines described above are explicitly labeled with the text **`- O.H.U.L. -`** (which the legend identifies as \"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE\").\n*   There is a continuous **`- O.H.U.L. -`** line running parallel to Valley View Road along the entire left frontage (Northern boundary) connecting the power poles.\n*   The service drop line crossing the property to the meter is also clearly labeled **`- O.H.U.L. -`**.\n\n**4. Electric Easements**\n*   The plan shows several utility easements around the perimeter of the property:\n    *   Along the top edge of the drawing (Eastern boundary): A dashed line is labeled **\"5' ELEC., TELE. & CABLE EASEMENT\"**.\n    *   Along the right edge of the drawing (Southern boundary): A dashed line is labeled **\"5' ELEC. EASEMENT\"**.\n    *   Along the bottom edge of the drawing (Western boundary): A dashed line is labeled **\"5' P.U.E.\"** (Public Utility Easement).\n\n**Summary of Findings:**\nOverhead utility lines and poles are clearly visible adjacent to Valley View Road. A primary overhead utility line (`- O.H.U.L. -`) runs along this road frontage. Notably, a secondary overhead service line branches from a pole on this frontage and routes directly across the property to connect to an electric meter on the existing structure.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReaso