{"level":30,"time":1776458356027,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify all overhead electric utility facilities shown. Specifically:\n1. Locate the overhead electric utility lines depicted on this sheet\n2. Identify the routing path of these lines across the site\n3. Note any buildings, structures, trees, or other site features that appear to be in proximity to the overhead lines\n4. Identify any trees proposed near overhead electric lines and note their species and locations\n5. Describe clearance dimensions or annotations related to overhead electric facilities (if shown)\n6. Note areas where overhead lines appear to cross over parking, driveways, or other site features\n\nProvide specific spatial descriptions of locations and relationships.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided landscape plan sheet, here are the findings regarding the overhead electric utility facilities:\n\n**1. Location of Overhead Electric Utility Lines**\nAn overhead electric utility line is depicted on this sheet. It is represented by a solid black line interspersed with the text exact text \"-OHE-\". This line is located along the extreme bottom edge of the drawing view. Based on the North arrow (pointing up), this corresponds to the southern boundary of the site plan area shown.\n\n**2. Routing Path Across the Site**\nThe \"-OHE-\" line runs in a straight horizontal path from the left (West) edge of the visible drawing area to the right (East) edge, running parallel to the bottom property/site boundary line.\n\n**3. Proximity to Site Features**\n*   **Building:** The main townhome building footprint is located to the north of the \"-OHE-\" line. The line runs parallel to the southern facade of the building, separated by a driveway and landscaped areas.\n*   **Driveway:** An internal driveway, denoted by lines with the text \"-SD-\", runs parallel to and north of the overhead electric line.\n*   **Sidewalk/Path:** A winding solid line, likely representing a sidewalk or path, runs closely parallel to the \"-OHE-\" line along the southern boundary, occasionally appearing to intersect or run directly underneath it.\n*   **Landscaping:** The line routes directly over areas designated for landscaping and sod (indicated by Key Note bubble \"H.7\").\n\n**4. Proposed Trees Near Overhead Electric Lines**\nThe routing path of the \"-OHE-\" line passes directly over or through several proposed tree locations (represented by circular symbols).\n*   **Species:** Specific tree species names (e.g., Oak, Elm) are **not listed** on this specific sheet, as there is no plant schedule table present.\n*   **Locations & Designations:** Near the bottom right (Southeast) corner of the drawing, the \"-OHE-\" line runs directly through a cluster of tree symbols. Specifically, it intersects:\n    *   One tree circle containing the exact letter \"**M**\". According to the text below the \"KEY NOTES\" section, \"M\" stands for \"M - MITIGATION TREE\".\n    *   One tree circle containing the exact letter \"**P**\". According to the text below the \"KEY NOTES\" section, \"P\" stands for \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\".\n*   Near the bottom left (Southwest) corner, the line passes very close to another tree circle associated with a callout bubble containing \"**H.8**\", though \"H.8\" is not defined in the provided Key Notes table.\n\n**5. Clearance Dimensions or Annotations**\nThere are **no** clearance dimensions, setback lines, or text annotations regarding required clearance from the overhead electric facilities depicted anywhere on this sheet.\n\n**6. Areas Where Overhead Lines Cross Site Features**\nBased on the plan view:\n*   The \"-OHE-\" line **does not** appear to cross over any internal parking spaces or the main internal drive aisle (\"-SD-\").\n*   It **does** cross directly over proposed landscape areas and specific proposed tree locations (as detailed in point 4).\n*   Near the bottom right corner, the \"-OHE-\" line crosses over a line designated \"-LOC-\" (typically Limits of Construction) and a line designated \"-W-\" (typically Water).","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1443,"outputTokens":719,"totalTokens":5035,"reasoningTokens":2873},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan and identify all overhead electric utility facilities shown. Specifically:\n1. Locate the over