{"level":30,"time":1776458356029,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":35,"prompt":"Identify the plant legend and specifically show: 1) What tree species symbols are used for mitigation trees (\"M\" designation). 2) The complete plant schedule showing all shade trees and ornamental trees with their common names, botanical names, and any utility-related notes. 3) Which specific trees are designated for mitigation plantings and their quantities. Look for any reference to utility-compatible trees or electrical clearance requirements.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the information requested:\n\n### 1) Tree Species Symbols for Mitigation (\"M\" Designation)\nThere are **no tree species symbols with an \"M\" designation** or any explicit mitigation-specific symbol variants in the \"PLANT LIST\" legend on this page. Mitigation is instead calculated mathematically as an aggregate surplus of all proposed tree inches on the site, rather than by tagging individual trees with an \"M\" symbol (see section 3 below for the exact calculation). \n\n### 2) Complete Plant Schedule (Shade and Ornamental Trees)\nBelow is the exact character-by-character transcription of the shade and ornamental tree sections from the \"PLANT LIST\" table. \n\n*Note: There are no utility-related notes present within or adjacent to this plant schedule.*\n\n**SHADE TREES**\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [Circle with dot] | | EXISTING TREE, TO BE PRESERVED | |\n| [Circle with cross] | 2 | LIVE OAK,<br>QUERCUS VIRGINIANA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL.,<br>16' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n| [Circle with grid] | 10 | CEDAR ELM,<br>ULMUS CRASSIFOLIA | 100 GAL., 4\" CAL.,<br>16' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n\n**ORNAMENTAL TREES**\n| SYM. | QTY. | COMMON NAME, BOTANICAL NAME | MIN. SPEC. |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| [Scalloped circle with dot] | 2 | TEXAS MOUNTAIN LAUREL,<br>SOPHORA SECUNDIFLORA | 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL.,<br>8' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n| [Scalloped circle with '8'] | 6 | MEXICAN REDBUD,<br>CERCIS CANADENSIS VAR. MEXICANA | 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL.,<br>10' HT. MINIMUM<br>CONTAINER<br>GROWN |\n\n### 3) Specific Trees Designated for Mitigation Plantings and Quantities\nIndividual trees are not separated into distinct \"mitigation\" vs \"landscape\" categories on the plant schedule. Instead, the document calculates mitigation mathematically using all proposed trees. \n\nAccording to the **\"COA REQUIRED TREES CHART\"** (bottom center), the entire proposed plant list is grouped to calculate mitigation inches:\n*   **Total tree inches required:** `A = 13` (Derived from 7.5\" Street Yard + 2.5\" Buffer + 3\" Parking Lot).\n*   **PER PLANT LIST:** `12 @ 4\"` and `8 @ 2.5\"` equals a total proposed inch count of `B = 68`. \n    *(Note: This perfectly matches the sum total of all shade and ornamental trees on the plant list: 12 Shade Trees at 4\" CAL. and 8 Ornamental Trees at 2.5\" CAL).*\n*   **PROPOSED TREE INCHES THAT MAY BE COUNTED FOR MITIGATION:** `(B-A)` results in `C = 55`.\n\nAdditionally, the **\"CITY OF AUSTIN TREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS:\"** table confirms this exact quantity under its final lines:\n*   `TOTAL MITIGATION INCHES PLANTED ON SITE` : `55 INCHES`\n\n**Summary of Mitigation Quantities:** All 20 new trees proposed on the project (12 Shade, 8 Ornamental) provide a combined 68 total caliper inches. After subtracting the 13 inches required for standard site landscaping, the remaining **55 inches** are collectively designated as the mitigation planting quantity.\n\n### 4) Utility-Compatible Trees or Electrical Clearance Requirements\nAfter a thorough review of all tables, calculations, and general notes (including \"REMEDIAL TREE CARE NOTES\", \"SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\", and \"SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT LANDSCAPE NOTES\" on this sheet), **there are no references to utility-compatible trees or electrical clearance requirements.** If this information exists, it is not present on this specific page of the plan set.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1394,"outputTokens":944,"totalTokens":6120,"reasoningTokens":3782},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2584864]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Identify the plant legend and specifically show: 1) What tree species symbols are used for mitigation trees (\"M\" designation). 2) The complete plant sche