n the interior courtyard areas.\n\n**3) Trees within 10 feet of overhead distribution lines or 50 feet of overhead transmission lines:**\n*   The plan does not distinguish whether the \"--OHE--\" line is distribution or transmission.\n*   However, there is a row of **five (5) trees** proposed along the southern property boundary that appear to be planted directly underneath or immediately adjacent to the \"--OHE--\" routing.\n*   All five of these trees are labeled exactly as **\"M\"** (Mitigation trees).\n*   Given the drawing scale indicated at the bottom right (\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"), these five trees are placed well within a 10-foot radius of the OHE line path.\n\n**4) Visible or identified tree species:**\n*   **No tree species are identified on this drawing.**\n*   There are no plant schedules, botanical names, or common names provided on this sheet. Trees are only identified by their function (SY, PL, M, P) as defined in the Key Notes legend.\n\n**5) Landscape features (fences, structures) near overhead lines:**\n*   A fence line, indicated by a line with intermittent \"X\" marks (---x---), runs along the entire southern property boundary parallel to the \"--OHE--\" line.\n*   According to the Key Notes, this line type (H-6) represents a **\"WOODEN PRIVACY FENCE\"**.\n*   This wooden privacy fence is located immediately adjacent to the overhead electric line routing on the southern edge of the site, separating the adjacent property from the row of five \"M\" trees and the southernmost building structures."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2571f496-befa-43e1-bc2b-06222dd9dc2e","uuid":"fc771bb0-0b1e-4050-87b8-c1b86d81c430","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan, here is the information regarding proposed trees and overhead electric lines (OHE):\n\n**1) Routing of overhead electric lines (OHE) on the site:**\n*   An overhead electric line, denoted by the line type \"--OHE--\", is 