{"level":30,"time":1776458363922,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011XPdju2cjHrdRxfNC1ixh3","type":"tool_result","content":"workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/facts.md:10:- **Easement (Greenbelt Access & Use, Instrument 2010070731):** A perpetual, no-build greenbelt easement covering 0.31 acres (13,524 sq ft) of the NE interior of Lot 1 is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer. County clerk research confirms it is real, recorded, and perpetual. Must be depicted before approval.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/facts.md:11:- **Easement (City of Austin Drainage, Instrument 2011021137):** A perpetual City of Austin drainage easement covering 0.130 acres (5,670 sq ft) of the NE corner of Lot 1 is NOT depicted on the submitted site plan and is NOT in the COA GIS easement layer. County clerk research confirms it is real, recorded, and perpetual. Must be depicted before approval.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/facts.md:99:- **Status on Site Plan:** Not depicted — must be added before approval\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/facts.md:108:- **Status on Site Plan:** Not depicted — must be added before approval; requires Watershed Protection coordination\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/tia-determination-worksheet/03-tpw-staff-determination.md:22:NOTE: A TIA determination must be made prior to submittal of any Zoning or Site Plan application; therefore, this completed and reviewed worksheet must accompany any subsequent application for the identical project. Changes to the proposed project may require a new TIA determination. This worksheet will remain valid for 90 calendar days from the approval date above, after which a new TIA Determination Worksheet will be required.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/project-review-form/02-information-required-for-vested-rights-review.md:7:In addition to providing the information below, attach a completed Vested Rights Petition (VRP) and supporting documentation, including project history from the Original Application to the present, with a copy of the original application for which vested rights are claimed and any subsequent permits or approvals issued for the property.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-02/guide.md:21:    The main drawing area containing the historical plat map, legal descriptions, owner's dedication, surveyor's certification, and approval signatures. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/consolidated-site-plan-application/01-project-information.md:12:This application is for obtaining Completeness Check Review approval for a consolidated site plan permit or a revision to a consolidated site plan permit within the City of Austin’s jurisdiction [full-purpose and limited purpose].\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/06-austin-energy-review.md:5:**CC Austin Energy Review** - Victor Givens - victor.givens@austinenergy.com\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:10:* U0: Payment of the site plan environmental inspection fee is required prior to permit/site plan approval. The fee is payable through the AB+C portal. EV Review will be approved prior to payment of this fee. However, the applicant is advised that the permit issuance will not occur until this fee has been paid. The case manager will confirm payment of the environmental inspection fee prior to permit issuance. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:15:* U0: Payment of the landscape inspection fee is required prior to permit/site plan approval. The fee is payable through the AB+C portal. EV Review will be approved prior to payment of this fee. However, the applicant is advised that the permit issuance will not occur until this fee has been paid. The case manager will confirm payment of the landscape inspection fee prior to permit issuance. \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/05-environmental-review.md:20:* U0: Provide a fiscal estimate for erosion/sedimentation controls and revegetation based on ECM Appendix S-1. For sites with a limit of construction greater than one acre, the fiscal estimate must include a $3000 per acre of LOC clean-up fee. The approved amount must be posted with the City prior to permit/site plan approval. [LDC 25-8-186, ECM 1.2.1, ECM Appendix S-1] \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/04-land-development-engineering-review.md:15:An **Encroachment Agreement** is needed for items that will be permanently placed within the City of Austin Right of Way (ROW) and shall be executed prior to issuance of the development permit. Encroachment Agreements require approval by City Council. City Code Chapter 14-11 \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/04-land-development-engineering-review.md:20:For development applications needing City of Austin **Easement Releases** prior to approval. City Code Chapter 14-11\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/04-land-development-engineering-review.md:24:For development applications needing City of Austin **ROW Vacations** prior to approval. City Code Chapter 14-11\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/04-land-development-engineering-review.md:27:➢ City Council approval is required.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-02/block-1.md:3:## drawing: The main content area showing the plat for the Mecey Subdivision. This includes the legal description, owner's dedication, surveyor's certification, approval signatures from the City Planning Commission, and filing records for Travis County. It features a map with property lines, dimensions, bearings, and curve data, along with a legend and scale. Notably, it contains handwritten signatures and stamps.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/08-pard-planning-design-review.md:10:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/overview.md:24:   File: `06-austin-energy-review.md`\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/12-water-quality-review.md:55:* U1: Comment pending environmental approval.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/completeness-check-results/02-drainage-and-water-quality-review.md:31:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/09-site-plan-review.md:36:U0: Include the following note with Figure 34 on the site plan page: \"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded in compliance with Subchapter E 2.5 and will be reviewed during building plan review. Any change or substitution of lamp/light fixtures shall be submitted to the Director for approval in accordance with Section 2.5.2.E.\" \nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/09-site-plan-review.md:46:a. All improvements shall be made in accordance with the released site plan. Any additional improvements will require site plan amendment and approval of the Development Ser