 or scarifying to a depth of at least two (2) inches prior to placement of six (6) inches of topsoil. [ECM 1.4.7, Appendix P-1]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-05/blocks.md:32:3. Permanent vegetative stabilization of areas disturbed by construction shall be per ECM Appendix P-1, unless otherwise indicated on the plan.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-06/blocks.md:43:2. All disturbed areas to be revegetated are required to have a minimum of six (6) inches of topsoil. Topsoil shall meet the definition in Standard Specification 601S.3. In areas where no topsoil exists, or where topsoil is needed for vegetative establishment, the subgrade shall be loosened by discing or scarifying to a depth of at least two (2) inches prior to placement of six (6) inches of topsoil. [ECM 1.4.7, Appendix P-1]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-06/blocks.md:44:3. Permanent vegetative stabilization of areas disturbed by construction shall be per ECM Appendix P-1, unless otherwise indicated on the plan.\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-06/block-10.md:7:[Omitted long matching line]\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/block-4.md:42:Wastewater service for this project can be provided based upon plan approval within the Austin Water\nworkspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-18/block-4.md:47:accepted by DSD, then this letter expires on the date the development application, or its approval, expires.","numLines":50,"appliedLimit":50}}
