{"level":30,"time":1776458474981,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UZwy6YHJfFtnrrF2MVRUk7","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"0b12a07a-5de8-44d8-95a3-433528e88826","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/wnavey/code/controlroom/conductor/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776458474981,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CiybTDLrSR9Y66t7rkT6Ah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! The electric review lists the applicable Austin Energy codes:\n- **UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees**\n- **Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual**\n\nThese are exactly the codes referenced in my grouping file! The electric review states that the site is subject to:\n- UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 for landscaping and trees (which is the same as the grouping's \"UCM § 1.10.10.4\")\n- ECM Appendix F for tree species specifications\n\nNow I need to research the utility compatibility of the specific tree species being proposed. The grouping specified that utility-compatible status comes from ECM Appendix F. Let me use a general-purpose agent to research the utility compatibility of these specific tree species based on ECM Appendix F standards.\n\n**Tree species to research:**\n1. Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 2 plants\n2. Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 10 plants\n3. Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) - 2 plants\n4. Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) - 6 plants\n\n**Also need to determine:**\n- Mature heights of each species\n- Whether they are listed as utility-compatible in ECM Appendix F\n- Whether any are in the 40+ foot large tree category","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1130,"cache_read_input_tokens":62799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1130},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"1eebd370-95d9-47a1-bff7-927d96b7f96a"}
