{"level":30,"time":1776458474981,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01CiybTDLrSR9Y66t7rkT6Ah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Research ECM Appendix F utility compatibility","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Research the utility compatibility status and mature heights of these four tree species according to City of Austin Environmental Criteria Manual (ECM) Appendix F:\n\n1. Live Oak (Quercus virginiana)\n2. Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia)\n3. Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora)\n4. Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana)\n\nFor each species, find:\n- Whether it has a \"UC\" (utility-compatible) designation in ECM Appendix F\n- The listed mature height per ECM Appendix F\n- Whether it qualifies as a \"large tree\" (40+ feet) for electrical utility purposes per UCM § 1.10.10.4\n- Any specific electrical clearance restrictions\n\nSearch for the most current version of Austin's ECM Appendix F and ECM 2.4.1 and 2.4.2 which reference utility-compatible trees."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1130,"cache_read_input_tokens":62799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1130},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"74f21549-6529-4cf9-86f8-ea2439eadc04"}
