{"level":30,"time":1776458474982,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jr4zXBYEqNTUc2T7MoGjp6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Austin ECM 2.4.1 2.4.2 utility-compatible trees electrical clearance\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Environmental Criteria Manual | Austin, TX - Municode Library\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/environmental_criteria_manual\"},{\"title\":\"CITY OF AUSTIN – DEVELOPMENT SERVICES DEPARTMENT\",\"url\":\"https://zilkerneighborhood.org/dev/1209AzieMorton/1209AzieMorton-site_plan_MRC0_(2020-03-05).pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Tree Trimming\",\"url\":\"https://austinenergy.com/residential/residential-services/tree-trimming\"},{\"title\":\"City of Austin Electric Utility Austin Energy Design Criteria\",\"url\":\"https://austinenergy.com/-/media/project/websites/austinenergy/contractors/designcriteriamanual.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Significant Tree Identification\",\"url\":\"https://services.austintexas.gov/edims/document.cfm?id=375574\"},{\"title\":\"City of Austin | Residential New Construction and Addition Permit Application\",\"url\":\"https://www.austintexas.gov/sites/default/files/files/Development_Services/RES_NewConstructionAndAdditionPermitApplication.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SUBDIVISION REVIEW SHEET CASE NO.: C8-2016-0234.0A PC DATE: January 9, 2018\",\"url\":\"https://services.austintexas.gov/edims/document.cfm?id=290794\"},{\"title\":\"4.Backup_JSC_Presentation on Tree Regulations and Protections_241023 | Joint Sustainability Committee\",\"url\":\"https://bandc.crccheck.com/jsc/439629-4backup_jsc_presentation-on-tree-regulations-and-protections_241023/\"},{\"title\":\"'We'll be working with our policymakers' | Austin power line tree trimming rules may be re-evaluated | kvue.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.kvue.com/article/news/investigations/defenders/austin-power-line-tree-trimming-rules-reevaluated/269-d57e1ba8-ed90-4fbf-aa7a-7aa6d705389a\"},{\"title\":\"Environmental Criteria Manual, Austin\",\"url\":\"http://austin-tx.elaws.us/code/ecm\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about utility-compatible trees and electrical clearance requirements in Austin's Environmental Criteria Manual (ECM).\n\nTrees from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list are required to be planted within 10 lateral feet from any overhead distribution conductor and 30 to 40 lateral feet from any overhead transmission conductor.\n\nThe search results indicate that mitigation planting must be of a species listed in ECM Appendix F and comply with planting criteria in ECM 3.5.4.B.1. This appendix contains the utility-compatible trees list referenced in the regulations.\n\nFor more specific details about sections ECM 2.4.1 and 2.4.2, you would need to access the full Austin Environmental Criteria Manual directly, as the search results don't provide the complete text of those particular sections. The Municipal Code Library link (source 1) appears to host the full ECM document and would have the detailed requirements you're looking for.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"e6d9411f-d6c7-44cf-ad79-1ef5fdfbfc7f"}
{"level":30,"time":1776458474982,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014xvbJaDr5ncEPJG77pgn9D","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"ECM Appendix F\" Austin Texas tree species mature height\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Significant Tree Identification\",\"url\":\"https://services.austintexas.gov/edims/document.cfm?id=375574\"},{\"title\":\"Section 3 - Tree and Natural Area Preservation\",\"url\":\"https://services.austintexas.gov/edims/document.cfm?id=357827\"},{\"title\":\"Environmental Criteria Manual | Austin, TX - Municode Library\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/environmental_criteria_manual\"},{\"title\":\"Environmental Criteria Manual - Section 3 (Tree and Natural Area Preservation)- 2021 2nd Quarter Rule Changes | SpeakUp Austin!\",\"url\":\"https://speakupaustin.us.engagementhq.com/dsd-environmental-criteria-manual-section-3-trees-2021-2nd-quarter-rule-changes\"},{\"title\":\"20241106-005: Austin Tree Regulation Presentation | Environmental Commission\",\"url\":\"https://bandc.crccheck.com/envboard/440150-20241106-005-austin-tree-regulation-presentation/\"},{\"title\":\"§ 3.3.2. General Tree Survey Standards, Appendix 3.3.0. TREE SURVEYS, Section 3. TREE AND NATURAL AREA PRESERVATION, Environmental Criteria Manual, Austin\",\"url\":\"http://austin-tx.elaws.us/code/ecm_sects3_3.3.0_sec3.3.2\"},{\"title\":\"Tree Ordinance Review Application\",\"url\":\"https://www.austintexas.gov/sites/default/files/files/Planning/City_Arborist/tree_permit_digital.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"APPENDIX F | Environmental Criteria Manual | Austin, TX\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/environmental_criteria_manual?nodeId=APXFDECATRSP\"},{\"title\":\"HEADS UP! CODES CHANGE! For updated cards and more detailed information,\",\"url\":\"https://aiaaustin.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/AIAAustinHousing_CodeCards_Card3_v1.00.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Appendix N. CITY OF AUSTIN PREFERRED PLANT LIST, Environmental Criteria Manual, Austin\",\"url\":\"http://austin-tx.elaws.us/code/ecm_appn\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found references to ECM (Environmental Criteria Manual) Appendix F from the City of Austin, which relates to tree species. The chart in Appendix F indicates how each species fits in a general classification, and Appendix F provides specific categorization such as tree, soil, site, or regulatory qualities.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain the actual detailed contents of Appendix F with specific tree species and their mature heights. The results reference that Appendix F exists and is used for tree species classifications in Austin's tree preservation requirements, but the actual chart with mature height data is not displayed in these search results.\n\nTo access the complete Appendix F with specific tree species and mature height information, you would need to consult the full Environmental Criteria Manual document directly from the City of Austin's website, particularly through their official ECM documentation or the Municode library entry for Austin's Environmental Criteria Manual.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"2b7af8d8-2869-4644-97f2-22542ee3c15a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776458474982,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UoqbLis9ojy1vKzG3bxQPS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"City of Austin Environmental Criteria Manual ECM Appendix F tree utility compatible UC designation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Environmental Criteria Manual | Austin, TX - Municode Library\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/environmental_criteria_manual\"},{\"title\":\"Environmental Criteria Manual, Austin\",\"url\":\"http://austin-tx.elaws.us/code/ecm\"},{\"title\":\"Ordinances for Austin, TX Environmental Criteria Manual\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/ordinances/environmental_criteria_manual\"},{\"title\":\"20241106-005: Austin Tree Regulation Presentation | Environmental Commission\",\"url\":\"https://bandc.crccheck.com/envboard/440150-20241106-005-austin-tree-regulation-presentation/\"},{\"title\":\"4.Backup_JSC_Presentation on Tree Regulations and Protections_241023 | Joint Sustainability Committee\",\"url\":\"https://bandc.crccheck.com/jsc/439629-4backup_jsc_presentation-on-tree-regulations-and-protections_241023/\"},{\"title\":\"1.3.0 | Environmental Criteria Manual | Austin, TX\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/environmental_criteria_manual?nodeId=S1WAQUMA_1.3.0ENREIN_1.3.1ENREINERRE\"},{\"title\":\"PREFACE, ENVIRONMENTAL CRITERIA MANUAL, Environmental Criteria Manual, Austin\",\"url\":\"http://austin-tx.elaws.us/code/ecm_encrma_pr\"},{\"title\":\"§ 2.4.1. Street Yard, Appendix 2.4.0. BASIC REQUIREMENTS, Section 2. LANDSCAPE, Environmental Criteria Manual, Austin\",\"url\":\"http://austin-tx.elaws.us/code/ecm_sects2_2.4.0_sec2.4.1\"},{\"title\":\"APPENDIX F | Environmental Criteria Manual | Austin, TX\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/environmental_criteria_manual?nodeId=APXFDECATRSP\"},{\"title\":\"ENVIRONMENTAL + SUSTAINABILITY\",\"url\":\"https://aiaaustin.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/AIAAustinHousing_CodeCards_Card3_v1.00.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information related to your query about the City of Austin Environmental Criteria Manual (ECM) Appendix F and tree utility compatibility:\n\nIn areas where utility lines are present or proposed, only trees from the Utility Compatible Shade Trees list (see Appendix F) shall be planted within 10 lateral feet from any overhead distribution conductor or 30 to 40 lateral feet from any overhead transmission conductor.\n\nThe search results indicate that mitigation planting must be of a species listed in ECM Appendix F, and this list includes designations for trees suitable for planting in utility-compatible situations.\n\nThe actual detailed UC (Utility Compatible) designation specifications and complete listings would be found in ECM Appendix F itself. The search results reference these requirements but don't provide the full contents of Appendix F with the specific UC designation criteria. To view the complete Appendix F with all utility-compatible tree designations, you would need to access the full Environmental Criteria Manual directly through the City of Austin's official documentation or the Municode library links referenced in the search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"d403aad9-2e50-40e7-a497-1d4bd964bfbc"}
{"level":30,"time":1776458474982,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NSYXvpHszcpYKPoAGbn7si","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Austin UCM 1.10.10.4 large tree 40 feet electrical utility\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"§ 1.1.0. INTRODUCTION, Section 1. AUSTIN ENERGY DESIGN CRITERIA, Utilities Criteria Manual, Austin\",\"url\":\"http://www.austin-tx.elaws.us/code/ucm_sects1_sec1.1.0\"},{\"title\":\"AUSTIN\",\"url\":\"https://coautilities.com/wps/wcm/connect/occ/21d8aeaf-0f41-4364-951f-3113bd166fbe/OCT_19_AUNow_ENG.pdf?MOD=AJPERES&CONVERT_TO=url&CACHEID=ROOTWORKSPACE.Z18_G0L8HOC0LGEC40AMK6T8400004-21d8aeaf-0f41-4364-951f-3113bd166fbe-mS5I8YF\"},{\"title\":\"1.10.0 | Utilities Criteria Manual | Austin, TX - Municode Library\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/utilities_criteria_manual?nodeId=S1AUENDECR_1.10.0CLSARE\"},{\"title\":\"Utilities Criteria Manual | Austin, TX - Municode Library\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/utilities_criteria_manual\"},{\"title\":\"R161-19.07 Austin Energy proposed changes to Utilities Criteria Manual\",\"url\":\"https://www.austintexas.gov/sites/default/files/files/R161-19.07_-_Utilities_Criteria_Manual_Edits_-_Section_1.9.0_METERING.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"City Electrical Code and Inspections ... - AustinTexas.gov\",\"url\":\"https://services.austintexas.gov/edims/document.cfm?id=312726\"},{\"title\":\"R161-19.03 Austin Energy proposed edits to Utilities Criteria Manual\",\"url\":\"https://www.austintexas.gov/sites/default/files/files/Draft_Edits_-_R161-19.03_-_AW_-_UCM.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"FAQs\",\"url\":\"https://austinenergy.com/residential/residential-services/tree-trimming/faqs\"},{\"title\":\"City of Austin Electric Utility Austin Energy Design Criteria\",\"url\":\"https://austinenergy.com/-/media/project/websites/austinenergy/contractors/designcriteriamanual.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"1.7.0 - TEMPORARY DISTRIBUTION POWER | Austin, TX\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/utilities_criteria_manual?nodeId=S1AUENDECR_1.7.0TEDIPO\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information related to your query about large trees and electrical utility clearances in Austin:\n\nFor trees with a mature height of 40+ feet, they should be planted at least 50 feet from a pole. Additionally, trees within 20 feet of power lines should be smaller — less than 25 feet high fully grown.\n\nThe search results indicate these are guidelines from Austin's utilities and tree planting documentation. However, the specific UCM section 1.10.10.4 was referenced in the search results but the detailed content of that particular section wasn't fully displayed in the available information. The results suggest that Section 1.10.0 covers clearance requirements for equipment, which may be related to your query.\n\nIf you need the specific details from UCM section 1.10.10.4, you may want to consult the full Austin Utilities Criteria Manual directly through the official City of Austin resources or Municode Library.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"6b353385-d9be-46de-891b-12b3fb9c5ea1"}
