{"level":30,"time":1776458474984,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"For each of the 5 transformer pads shown on this electrical plan, provide:\n\n1. TRANSFORMER SERVICE TYPE: Is the service type (single-phase or three-phase) indicated anywhere on the plan for each transformer? Look for any annotations, callouts, or specifications indicating service type.\n\n2. PAD DIMENSIONS AND DETAILS: Are the dimensions of the transformer pads shown? Are there any reference callouts to AE Design detail sheets or specifications?\n\n3. UTILITY SEPARATIONS: Show the proximity and clearances (if dimensioned) from the transformer pads to:\n   - Underground water lines (if shown)\n   - Underground wastewater lines (if shown)\n   - Storm drain lines (if shown)\n   - Other underground utilities\n\n4. ACCESS DOOR ORIENTATION: For each transformer, which direction does the access door face (if discernible from the drawing)?\n\n5. EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS: Are there any notes about oil-filled vs. dry-type transformer specifications?\n\n6. PARKING/TRAFFIC PROXIMITY: Estimate distance from each transformer pad to the nearest parking space, drive aisle, or circulation route.\n\n7. EASEMENT INFORMATION: What easements are shown near each transformer location?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan,\" here is the specific information for each of the 5 transformer pads shown on the document. \n\nAll 5 transformer pads are labeled uniformly with a callout reading exactly **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** pointing to a cross-hatched rectangle. \n\n***\n\n### 1. Transformer Pad (Northwest - Near Bldg. 1)\nLocated west of Bldg. 1, near Unit 101.\n\n1. **TRANSFORMER SERVICE TYPE:** Not indicated. There are no annotations or specifications on this sheet detailing whether it is single-phase or three-phase.\n2. **PAD DIMENSIONS AND DETAILS:** Not indicated. The pad is drawn as a cross-hatched rectangle, but no dimensions (e.g., length/width) are provided. There are no reference callouts to AE Design detail sheets or specifications.\n3. **UTILITY SEPARATIONS:** Clearances are not dimensioned.\n   * **Underground water lines:** A water line (\"W\" with dashed line) runs parallel to the property line to the west. Visual estimate puts it approximately 15-20 feet west of the pad.\n   * **Underground wastewater lines:** None visible immediately adjacent.\n   * **Storm drain lines:** A storm drain line (\"SD\") and an inlet box are located immediately south/southeast of the pad.\n   * **Other:** Underground electric lines (solid blue line) connect directly to the pad.\n4. **ACCESS DOOR ORIENTATION:** Not discernible from the drawing. The symbol is a uniform cross-hatched rectangle with no indicators for a front or access side.\n5. **EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS:** Not indicated. There are no notes specifying oil-filled vs. dry-type.\n6. **PARKING/TRAFFIC PROXIMITY:** Visually estimated (based on the 1\"=20' scale) to be approximately 10-15 feet from the back of the curb of the western street (Valley View Road). It is separated from the street by a sidewalk and grassy area.\n7. **EASEMENT INFORMATION:** A **\"Sidewalk Easement\"** is located to the west between the pad and the street. \n\n### 2. Transformer Pad (Mid-West - Near Bldg. 2)\nLocated west of Bldg. 2, near Unit 201.\n\n1. **TRANSFORMER SERVICE TYPE:** Not indicated.\n2. **PAD DIMENSIONS AND DETAILS:** Not indicated. No dimensions or AE Design callouts are present.\n3. **UTILITY SEPARATIONS:** Clearances are not dimensioned.\n   * **Underground water lines:** A water line (\"W\") is located further west, past the sidewalk.\n   * **Underground wastewater lines:** None visible immediately adjacent.\n   * **Storm drain lines:** A storm drain line (\"SD\") runs north-south between the transformer pad and the building.\n   * **Other:** Underground electric lines connect directly to the pad.\n4. **ACCESS DOOR ORIENTATION:** Not discernible from the drawing.\n5. **EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS:** Not indicated.\n6. **PARKING/TRAFFIC PROXIMITY:** Visually estimated to be approximately 15-20 feet east of the western street curb (Valley View Road), with a sidewalk in between.\n7. **EASEMENT INFORMATION:** A **\"Sidewalk Easement\"** is located to the west.\n\n### 3. Transformer Pad (Southwest - Near Bldg. 8)\nLocated west of Bldg. 8, near Unit 801.\n\n1. **TRANSFORMER SERVICE TYPE:** Not indicated.\n2. **PAD DIMENSIONS AND DETAILS:** Not indicated. No dimensions or AE Design callouts are present.\n3. **UTILITY SEPARATIONS:** Clearances are not dimensioned.\n   * **Underground water lines:** A water line (\"W\") is located to the west, past the sidewalk.\n   * **Underground wastewater lines:** None visible immediately adjacent.\n   * **Storm drain lines:** A storm drain line (\"SD\") runs north-south between the transformer pad and the building.\n   * **Other:** Underground electric lines connect directly to the pad.\n4. **ACCESS DOOR ORIENTATION:** Not discernible from the drawing.\n5. **EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS:** Not indicated.\n6. **PARKING/TRAFFIC PROXIMITY:** Visually estimated to be approximately 15-20 feet east of the western street curb (Valley View Road), with a sidewalk in between.\n7. **EASEMENT INFORMATION:** A **\"Sidewalk Easement\"** is located to the west.\n\n### 4. Transformer Pad (Southeast - Between Bldg. 6 & Bldg. 7)\nLocated on the east side of the property, in the recessed area between Bldg. 6 and Bldg. 7.\n\n1. **TRANSFORMER SERVICE TYPE:** Not indicated.\n2. **PAD DIMENSIONS AND DETAILS:** Not indicated. No dimensions or AE Design callouts are present.\n3. **UTILITY SEPARATIONS:** Clearances are not dimensioned.\n   * **Underground water lines:** Main water lines appear to run under the internal drive aisle to the east.\n   * **Underground wastewater lines:** Wastewater lines appear to run under the internal drive aisle to the east.\n   * **Storm drain lines:** A storm drain line (\"SD\") and an inlet are located in close proximity just north of the pad.\n   * **Other:** Underground electric lines connect directly to the pad.\n4. **ACCESS DOOR ORIENTATION:** Not discernible from the drawing.\n5. **EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS:** Not indicated.\n6. **PARKING/TRAFFIC PROXIMITY:** This pad is located close to the internal drive aisle and parking area. Visual estimation puts it approximately 5-10 feet from the edge of the paved parking/drive surface.\n7. **EASEMENT INFORMATION:** There are broad utility easements along the eastern boundary. Text nearby reads **\"25' Drainage Easement ... P.U.E. & P.K.T.C.T.\"** but the exact boundary line relative to the pad's footprint is difficult to ascertain with certainty.\n\n### 5. Transformer Pad (Mid-East - Near Bldg. 5)\nLocated east of Bldg. 5, near Unit 504.\n\n1. **TRANSFORMER SERVICE TYPE:** Not indicated.\n2. **PAD DIMENSIONS AND DETAILS:** Not indicated. No dimensions or AE Design callouts are present.\n3. **UTILITY SEPARATIONS:** Clearances are not dimensioned.\n   * **Underground water lines:** Main water lines appear to run under the internal drive aisle to the east.\n   * **Underground wastewater lines:** Wastewater lines appear to run under the internal drive aisle to the east.\n   * **Storm drain lines:** A storm drain line (\"SD\") runs nearby.\n   * **Other:** Underground electric lines connect directly to the pad.\n4. **ACCESS DOOR ORIENTATION:** Not discernible from the drawing.\n5. **EQUIPMENT SPECIFICATIONS:** Not indicated.\n6. **PARKING/TRAFFIC PROXIMITY:** Located adjacent to the internal drive aisle and parking area. Visual estimation puts it approximately 5-10 feet from the edge of the paved surface.\n7. **EASEMENT INFORMATION:** Similar to Pad 4, it is located near the eastern property boundary which contains a **\"25' Drainage Easement ... P.U.E. & P.K.T.C.T.\"**, though the exact bounds over the pad are not explicitly drawn.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1563,"outputTokens":1588,"totalTokens":6214,"reasoningTokens":3063},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"For each of the 5 transformer pads shown on this electrical plan, provide:\n\n1. TRANSFORMER SERVICE TYPE: Is the service type (single-phase or three-phase) indicated anywhere on the plan for each transformer? Look for any annotations, callouts, or specifications indicating service type.\n\n2. PAD DIMENSIONS AND DETAILS: Are the dimensions o