{"level":30,"time":1776458474985,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine Sheet 9 (Site Plan) for overhead electric infrastructure:\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Lines & Poles**: Are overhead electric distribution or transmission lines shown on this site plan? Look for dashed or solid lines labeled \"OHE\" or \"-OHE-\" that indicate overhead conductors. Are utility poles marked or depicted? If so, where are they located relative to the property boundaries (east, south, west, north sides)?\n\n2. **Voltage/Type Classification**: Are there any labels or markings that indicate whether the overhead lines are distribution (lower voltage) or transmission (higher voltage, 60kV or more)?\n\n3. **Line Routing**: If overhead electric lines are present, trace their routing. Do they run along the property boundary (along Valley View Road to the south, or another edge)?\n\n4. **Proximity to Buildings/Trees**: Are the overhead lines positioned close to any proposed buildings, parking areas, or tree locations?\n\n5. **Pole Positions**: If poles are shown, mark their approximate locations and estimate their distance from proposed building structures or the site boundary.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Site Plan), here are the details regarding the overhead electric infrastructure:\n\n1.  **Overhead Electric Lines & Poles**:\n    *   Yes, overhead electric lines are clearly shown on this site plan. \n    *   A dashed line labeled with **\"- OHE -\"** is visible running horizontally across the bottom of the drawing (which corresponds to the southern boundary of the site).\n    *   Utility poles are depicted as small circular symbols along this line. \n\n2.  **Voltage/Type Classification**:\n    *   There are **no labels, markings, or notes** visible on this specific sheet that classify the voltage of the overhead lines (e.g., no indication of whether it is a lower-voltage distribution line or a high-voltage transmission line like 69kV+).\n\n3.  **Line Routing**:\n    *   The **\"- OHE -\"** line runs primarily East-West along the entire southern boundary of the property. It appears to be located just on or slightly outside the southern property line, parallel to the site's boundary.\n\n4.  **Proximity to Buildings/Trees**:\n    *   **Buildings**: The closest proposed building to the overhead line is **\"Bldg. 8\"**. The line does not appear to cross over the building; it is separated from Bldg. 8 by a parking area, a drive aisle, and a proposed \"Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n    *   **Trees**: There are several existing tree symbols (scalloped circles) depicted near the southern boundary line in close proximity to the \"- OHE -\" line, particularly near the southwest and southeast corners of the site.\n\n5.  **Pole Positions**:\n    *   Utility pole symbols are positioned at intermittent points along the southern \"- OHE -\" line:\n        *   One pole is located near the bottom-left (southwest) corner of the site, just west of the note \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\".\n        *   Another pole is located near the bottom-center of the property line, directly south of the parking area for Bldg. 8.\n        *   A third pole is visible near the bottom-right (southeast) corner of the property line, near the area labeled \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement\".\n    *   Exact distances from the poles to the buildings are not explicitly dimensioned on this plan, but they are situated well outside the building footprints, beyond the parking and retaining wall areas at the southern perimeter.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1535,"outputTokens":523,"totalTokens":4740,"reasoningTokens":2682},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jp