{"level":30,"time":1776458474986,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine this site plan and answer the following questions about the proposed development relative to existing overhead utilities:\n\n1. Are there any notes, dimensions, or callouts on this site plan showing clearances from existing overhead electric utilities or power poles?\n\n2. What is the relative location and distance of the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) from Valley View Road? How close do any buildings come to the Valley View Road frontage where the overhead utility poles and lines are located (based on the existing conditions survey)?\n\n3. Are there any dimension lines, distance callouts, or technical notes indicating clearances (horizontal or vertical) from overhead lines to buildings, parking areas, driveways, or other structures?\n\n4. Is there any indication that proposed utilities are underground vs. overhead?\n\n5. Are there any sections, profiles, or elevation views referenced that might show vertical clearances from overhead lines?\n\nPlease provide specific observations from the plan.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided site plan for Valley View Townhomes, here are the observations regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Notes, dimensions, or callouts showing clearances from existing overhead utilities:**\n*   Existing overhead electric lines are explicitly drawn and labeled with the line type **`--- OHE ---`** along the northern (top of page) and southern (bottom of page) property boundaries. \n*   However, there are **no explicit notes, dimensions, or callouts** anywhere on this sheet that specify required horizontal or vertical clearances from these overhead utility lines or poles to the proposed structures.\n\n**2. Relative location and distance of proposed buildings from Valley View Road:**\n*   **Location:** Valley View Road is located on the western boundary of the site (the left side of the drawing). Buildings 1 and 8 are the closest proposed structures to this road frontage.\n*   **Distances:** \n    *   **Building 1** (top left) has a dimension line showing it is **`26.1'`** (feet) from the front property line adjacent to Valley View Road.\n    *   **Building 8** (bottom left) has a dimension line showing it is **`33.3'`** (feet) from the front property line adjacent to Valley View Road.\n*   **OHE Location Note:** Based on the existing conditions shown, the prominent **`--- OHE ---`** lines run perpendicular to Valley View Road, along the top and bottom property lines, rather than parallel along the immediate Valley View Road frontage. There are no overhead lines shown encroaching on the front setback between the road and Buildings 1 or 8.\n\n**3. Dimension lines or technical notes indicating clearances from overhead lines to structures:**\n*   There are **no dimension lines or technical notes** indicating specific utility clearances (horizontal or vertical) from the overhead lines to buildings, parking areas, driveways, or other structures. \n*   The plan does show standard property line setbacks (e.g., a dashed line labeled `25'` near Building 6, and building-to-building dimensions like `10.2'`), but none are labeled as clearance requirements for the overhead electric lines. Along the top boundary where an OHE line exists, a **`5' P.U.E.`** (Public Utility Easement) is called out, but a structural clearance distance is not provided.\n\n**4. Indication of proposed utilities being underground vs. overhead:**\n*   There is no explicit text note mandating that proposed dry utilities be underground. \n*   However, all proposed utility linework shown routing through the site is for standard underground infrastructure. This includes **`--- W ---`** (Water), **`--- WW ---`** (Wastewater), and **`--- SD ---`** (Storm Drain). \n*   There are **no proposed overhead lines** drawn on the plan for the new development.\n\n**5. Sections, profiles, or elevation views referencing vertical clearances:**\n*   There are **no sections, profiles, or elevation views** referenced on this plan that indicate vertical clearances for overhead lines. \n*   The only detail callouts present are for standard civil flatwork (e.g., \"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ) See Dtl 432S-1\" and \"Construct Type III Driveway See Detail 433S-2\").","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1501,"outputTokens":720,"totalTokens":5319,"reasoningTokens":3098},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant i