{"level":30,"time":1776459690484,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011xdDdrApDDk7GSfWVuuCY7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now submitted my findings. Let me review what I found:\n\n**FINDINGS (fail or not-verifiable only):**\n\n1. **EL-2.1 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Species UC status not documented\n2. **EL-2.3 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Mature heights not documented for proposed trees\n3. **EL-2.6 - FAIL**: Mitigation tree at 9.2 feet from pole (less than 10 ft minimum)\n4. **EL-2.12 - FAIL**: No dimensions/measurements of conductor distances on plans\n5. **EL-2.15 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Cannot determine if trees are in prohibited zones without UC/height info, and no Austin Energy approval found\n\n**ITEMS NOT FLAGGED (Pass or N/A):**\n- EL-2.2: No transmission lines indicated (N/A)\n- EL-2.4: No transmission lines indicated (N/A)\n- EL-2.5: No transmission easement boundaries shown; facts.md mentions existing easements but not clear if this applies (N/A)\n- EL-2.7: No pad-mounted equipment shown on landscape plan (N/A)\n- EL-2.8: Not checking this without clearer indication\n- EL-2.9: Not checking this without clearer indication\n- EL-2.10: Plant legend DOES identify species (PASS - not flagged)\n- EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated on plans - actually this could be FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE. Let me reconsider...\n\nActually, looking at EL-2.11: \"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) not differentiated on plans to allow verification of clearances from overhead electric facilities\"\n\nThe plant schedule lists trees but doesn't differentiate which ones are \"large\" (40+ ft mature height). \n\nThe landscape plan itself lacks any notation to distinguish large trees from smaller ones. Without documented mature heights, I can't verify which trees qualify as large, so this is NOT-VERIFIABLE rather than a clear failure. For EL-2.14, the trees and overhead facilities are both shown on the landscape plan, so that requirement appears satisfied.\n\nRegarding EL-2.13, I don't see clearance measurements marked on the plans at all—the trees are represented as symbols, and I measured from their center points representing planting locations. This seems acceptable. However, I should reconsider whether EL-2.11 warrants inclusion in my findings. The standard requires large trees to be differentiated on plans so clearances can be verified, but the landscape plan only shows tree species symbols without any notation indicating which ones are large trees based on mature height specifications.\n\nThe plant schedule lists species and quantities but doesn't explicitly state mature heights or categorize trees as large or small. While the shade trees shown (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) would likely exceed 40 feet and ornamental trees (Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) would likely be under 40 feet based on typical Austin standards, this distinction isn't documented on the plans or schedule. Since the grouping file identifies this as a \"Reviewer Convention,\" the applicant should be clearly differentiating large trees from small trees. I think I need to add EL-2.11 as a finding.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2321,"cache_read_input_tokens":77486,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2321},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebb5ab1e-5561-44cc-87a8-e1311e730c80","uuid":"bf089044-8fa0-4286-8bc6-25c06cdacc67"}
