{"level":30,"time":1776459690484,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01ViHquL7anxNb46V3aFUM11","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've now submitted my complete findings for the grouping. Let me summarize what I found:\n\n**VIOLATIONS IDENTIFIED (6 findings):**\n\n1. **EL-2.1 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Plant schedule doesn't document UC (utility-compatible) status for proposed trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel)\n\n2. **EL-2.3 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Plant schedule doesn't document mature heights for proposed trees that would show whether they exceed 40-foot threshold\n\n3. **EL-2.6 - FAIL**: Mitigation tree positioned only 9.2 feet from utility pole (less than required 10 feet)\n\n4. **EL-2.11 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Large trees are not differentiated on plans or in plant schedule\n\n5. **EL-2.12 - FAIL**: No dimensions or measurements shown on landscape plan to verify clearances from outside conductors\n\n6. **EL-2.15 - NOT-VERIFIABLE**: Cannot determine if trees are in prohibited zones without UC/height documentation, and no Austin Energy approval letter found\n\n**ITEMS EVALUATED AS PASS OR N/A (not flagged):**\n- EL-2.2: N/A - no transmission lines indicated\n- EL-2.4: N/A - no transmission lines indicated  \n- EL-2.5: N/A - no transmission easement on proposed site\n- EL-2.7: N/A - no pad-mounted equipment on landscape plan\n- EL-2.8: N/A or PASS - cannot confirm underground equipment near trees\n- EL-2.9: N/A - no underground equipment shown near trees with requirement for root barriers\n- EL-2.10: PASS - plant legend clearly identifies species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud, plus shrubs)\n\n\n- EL-2.13: PASS - tree locations measured from trunk symbols, not canopy edges\n- EL-2.14: PASS - trees ARE shown on landscape plan 