{"level":30,"time":1776459690484,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01ViHquL7anxNb46V3aFUM11","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary of Review Findings\n\nI have completed the review of Grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan. \n\n### Key Findings:\n\n**6 deficiencies identified:**\n\n1. **EL-2.1 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Utility-compatible status of proposed tree species (Cedar Elm, Live Oak, Mexican Redbud, Texas Mountain Laurel) is not documented. Cannot verify compliance with 15-foot clearance requirement for non-utility-compatible trees.\n\n2. **EL-2.3 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Mature heights per ECM Appendix F are not documented for proposed trees. Cannot verify which trees may exceed 40-foot threshold triggering additional 25-foot clearance requirements.\n\n3. **EL-2.6 (FAIL)**: A mitigation tree on the southeastern property boundary is positioned only 9.2 feet from a utility pole, violating the 10-foot minimum clearance requirement.\n\n4. **EL-2.11 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Large trees (40+ feet) are not differentiated on the landscape plan or in the plant schedule, preventing clear verification of clearance zone applicability.\n\n5. **EL-2.12 (FAIL)**: The landscape plan shows trees near overhead electric lines but provides no dimension lines, measurements, or notes verifying clearances from the outside conductor position. The plan does not account for conductor offset (4+ feet) from pole centerline.\n\n6. **EL-2.15 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)**: Without documented species compatibility and mature height specifications, cannot definitively determine if trees are within prohibited clearance zones. No Austin Energy written approval is visible in submitted documents.\n\n### Research Conducted:\n- Overhead electric distribution lines confirmed along southern property boundary (Sheets 9, 31)\n- Utility poles identified at three locations along property line\n- Proposed mitigation trees measured: 9.2 ft (southeast), 48.1 ft (southwest), 187.4 ft (center)\n- Plant species identified but lacking utility-compatibility and mature height documentation\n- Landscape and electrical plans show infrastructure but lack clearance verification dimensions\n\nThe review is complete."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2502,"cache_read_input_tokens":79807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2502},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ebb5ab1e-5561-44cc-87a8-e1311e730c80","uuid":"66d9534e-4bcb-41a4-ab7d-e35a1b07b11b"}
