{"level":30,"time":1776459690486,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019WfhZuxwjCt1WhGBqXDTbi","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Quercus virginiana\" \"Ulmus crassifolia\" \"Sophora secundiflora\" Austin ECM mature height\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Sophora secundiflora, mescal bean | US Forest Service Research and Development\",\"url\":\"https://research.fs.usda.gov/feis/species-reviews/sopsec\"},{\"title\":\"Quercus virginiana Mill\",\"url\":\"https://www.srs.fs.usda.gov/pubs/misc/ag_654/volume_2/quercus/virginiana.htm\"},{\"title\":\"Austin, TX USDA Hardiness Zone Map & Planting Schedule - The Garden Magazine\",\"url\":\"https://thegardenmagazine.com/austin-tx-usda-hardiness-zone-map-planting-schedule/\"},{\"title\":\"Quercus virginiana - Plant Finder\",\"url\":\"https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/PlantFinder/PlantFinderDetails.aspx?taxonid=280730\"},{\"title\":\"Coast Live Oak Quercus virginiana\",\"url\":\"http://texastreeid.tamu.edu/content/TreeDetails/?id=109\"},{\"title\":\"Lady Bird Johnson Wildflower Center - The University of Texas at Austin\",\"url\":\"https://www.wildflower.org/expert/show.php?id=4799\"},{\"title\":\"SPECIES: Quercus virginiana\",\"url\":\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/database/feis/plants/tree/quevir/all.html\"},{\"title\":\"Quercus virginiana (Southern live oak) | Native Plants of ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.wildflower.org/plants/result.php?id_plant=QUVI\"},{\"title\":\"Texas Live Oak Quercus fusiformis x virginiana — Oaktopia\",\"url\":\"https://www.oaktopia.org/species/texaslive\"},{\"title\":\"Fact Sheet ST-564 October 1994 Quercus virginiana\",\"url\":\"https://hort.ifas.ufl.edu/database/documents/pdf/tree_fact_sheets/quevira.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding these three species mentioned together in relation to Austin and East Central Mexico (ECM):\n\nThese three species commonly occur together in riparian deciduous forests in the Edwards Plateau and Rio Grande Plains regions, with Quercus virginiana (live oak), Ulmus crassifolia (cedar elm), and Sophora secundiflora (mescal bean) listed among associated species. All three are recommended for Austin, TX plantings.\n\nRegarding mature heights:\n\n- **Quercus virginiana (Live Oak)**: Commonly reaches 50 feet tall with a short, stout trunk, forming a low, dense crown that can spread more than 100 feet.\n\n- **Ulmus crassifolia (Cedar Elm)**: The search results did not contain specific mature height information for this species.\n\n- **Sophora secundiflora (Texas Mountain Laurel/Mescal Bean)**: The search results did not contain specific mature height information for this species.\n\nIf you need specific mature height data for cedar elm and mescal bean, I'd recommend consulting botanical databases or horticultural resources specifically focused on Texas native plants.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"15ce3576-8ea0-43e7-9369-41b0eb63313f"}
{"level":30,"time":1776459690486,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A7iDhGVRidHhYehHkPSWFd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Austin \"utility compatible shade trees\" list appendix F species mature height\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Residential Tree Planting List\",\"url\":\"https://www.austintexas.gov/sites/default/files/files/Planning/City_Arborist/RecommendedTreePlantingList.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Native shade trees for Austin | NPIN\",\"url\":\"https://www.wildflower.org/expert/show.php?id=3939&frontpage=true\"},{\"title\":\"Shade Tree Selections in Austin, TX | Ted’s Trees, Ltd.\",\"url\":\"https://www.tedstrees.com/our-tree-selection\"},{\"title\":\"APPENDIX F | Environmental Criteria Manual | Austin, TX\",\"url\":\"https://library.municode.com/tx/austin/codes/environmental_criteria_manual?nodeId=APXFDECATRSP\"},{\"title\":\"Top Trees for Austin Yards: Shade, Beauty & Easy Maintenance\",\"url\":\"https://www.agavetreeservicesaustin.com/post/top-trees-for-austin-yards-shade-beauty-easy-maintenance\"},{\"title\":\"5 Best Shade Trees for Austin | Top Choice Lawn Care\",\"url\":\"https://www.topchoiceaustin.com/best-shade-trees/\"},{\"title\":\"Shade Solutions: Best Trees and Pergolas for Austin Yards - Urban Oasis\",\"url\":\"https://urbanoasiscontracting.com/backyard-shade-design-austin-trees-pergolas/\"},{\"title\":\"Top Trees To Plant In Austin - Austin Tree Surgeons\",\"url\":\"https://austintreesurgeons.com/top-trees-to-plant-in-austin/\"},{\"title\":\"Austin Tree Requirements for Residential Subdivision - Smart Surfaces Policy Tracker\",\"url\":\"https://smartsurfacespolicy.org/policies/austin-tree-requirements-for-residential-subdivision/\"},{\"title\":\"Best Trees to Plant in Austin | Tree Surgeons of Austin\",\"url\":\"https://www.treesurgeonsofaustin.com/best-trees-to-plant-in-austin/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about Austin's tree requirements:\n\nThe tree planting list is based on commercially available trees that are found in the City of Austin's Appendix F, which is part of the Environmental Criteria Manual. For all residential subdivisions, each single family lot requires at least two trees of at least two different species listed in the city's Environmental Criteria Manual, Appendix F (Descriptive Categories of Tree Species).\n\nHowever, the search results don't provide the complete details of the specific \"utility compatible shade trees\" list from Appendix F with the detailed species and mature height information you're looking for. While I found a reference to Austin's Recommended Tree Planting List PDF from the City Arborist's office, the search results only show that such a list exists, not the full contents with species names and mature heights.\n\nTo access the complete Appendix F list with utility-compatible species and their mature heights, you would need to consult the Austin Environmental Criteria Manual directly or contact the City of Austin's Planning Department or City Arborist's office.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"beffe4dc-ba9c-483b-9647-430ff8ce993a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776459690486,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AgDDMSRWkYiZJNSBF6xDeg","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Cercis canadensis var. mexicana\" Austin tree height utility compatible\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Cercis canadensis var. mexicana | Landscape Plants | Oregon State University\",\"url\":\"https://landscapeplants.oregonstate.edu/plants/cercis-canadensis-var-mexicana\"},{\"title\":\"Cercis canadensis var. mexicana (Mexican redbud)\",\"url\":\"https://www.wildflower.org/plants/result.php?id_plant=cecam\"},{\"title\":\"Cercis canadensis subsp. mexicana (Mexican Redbud) | North Carolina Extension Gardener Plant Toolbox\",\"url\":\"https://plants.ces.ncsu.edu/plants/cercis-canadensis-subsp-mexicana/\"},{\"title\":\"Cercis canadensis var. mexicana - Native Plant Society of Texas\",\"url\":\"https://www.npsot.org/posts/native-plant/cercis-canadensis-var-mexicana/\"},{\"title\":\"Mexican Redbud, Cercis canadensis var. mexicana, Monrovia Plant\",\"url\":\"https://www.monrovia.com/mexican-redbud.html\"},{\"title\":\"Cercis canadensis var. texensis (Texas redbud)\",\"url\":\"https://www.wildflower.org/plants/result.php?id_plant=CECAT\"},{\"title\":\"Cercis Species, Mexican Redbud Cercis canadensis var. mexicana\",\"url\":\"https://davesgarden.com/guides/pf/go/97858/\"},{\"title\":\"Cercis canadensis var. mexicana | Cercis canadensis ssp. mexicana | Mexican Redbud | plant lust\",\"url\":\"https://plantlust.com/plants/18607/cercis-canadensis-var-mexicana/\"},{\"title\":\"Ufl\",\"url\":\"http://hort.ufl.edu/database/documents/pdf/tree_fact_sheets/cermexa.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Cercis canadensis\",\"url\":\"https://apps.cals.arizona.edu/arboretum/taxon.aspx?id=754\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about *Cercis canadensis* var. *mexicana* (Mexican redbud):\n\n## Height\n\nThis is a deciduous multi-stemmed shrub or small tree that grows 5-12 feet tall, though some sources indicate slightly larger mature sizes. Other measurements show it can grow 11 to 15 feet high and 11 to 15 feet wide, and another source indicates it reaches 12 to 20 feet tall.\n\n## Austin/Texas Suitability\n\nThe Mexican redbud is well-suited to Austin and the surrounding Texas region. It is one of three *Cercis canadensis* varieties naturally occurring in Texas, and is shorter and more compact in Texas than the others, more likely to have multiple trunks. It has low to medium water use, is drought tolerant, heat tolerant, and prefers alkaline soils.\n\n## Utility Compatibility\n\nThe search results do not contain specific information about utility compatibility (such as clearance requirements for power lines or underground utilities). However, it makes an attractive understory tree, accent tree, or shrub, and it is especially adapted to conditions in the southwest desert and works very well in a small space, suggesting it could be suitable for limited spaces where utility compatibility might be a concern. For detailed utility compatibility information, you may need to consult Austin-specific tree guides or the city's utility department.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPBPYGjbZDsqxm3Nv5ubF2","session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"3b56c828-7315-41b7-940f-66a7c448f3e5"}
