{"level":30,"time":1776460000009,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Examine the site plan and identify all proposed buildings, structures, and site features relative to any shown overhead electric facilities. Please describe: 1) the locations of all 8 buildings (Buildings 1-8) and their proximity to property boundaries, 2) any overhead electric utility lines shown on this plan and their routing, 3) the location of utility poles or overhead infrastructure, 4) retaining walls and their locations, 5) driveways and parking areas relative to any overhead lines, 6) whether any building overhangs, awnings, or canopies are shown extending toward overhead lines, 7) any clearance dimensions or notes related to overhead electric facilities. Use the main drawing area to identify features.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful examination of the provided site plan document, here is the detailed analysis addressing your specific questions regarding the relationship between proposed site features and overhead electric facilities:\n\n**1. Locations of all 8 buildings and their proximity to property boundaries:**\nThe site features 8 proposed buildings roughly distributed around a central internal driveway loop. Their locations relative to the heavy solid line denoting the property boundary are as follows:\n*   **Bldg. 1**: Located in the Northwest corner of the site, near the west and north property boundaries.\n*   **Bldg. 2**: Located on the West side of the site, south of Bldg. 1, near the west property boundary.\n*   **Bldg. 3**: Located in the North-central area, near the north property boundary.\n*   **Bldg. 4**: Located centrally within the site, surrounded by internal driveways.\n*   **Bldg. 5**: Located in the Northeast corner, near the north and east property boundaries.\n*   **Bldg. 6**: Located on the East side, south of Bldg. 5, near the east property boundary. A dimension of \"25'\" is shown between the building side and the eastern boundary area.\n*   **Bldg. 7**: Located in the South-central area, positioned near the south property boundary.\n*   **Bldg. 8**: Located in the Southwest corner, near the west and south property boundaries. A dimension of \"29.8'\" is shown from its southwest corner toward the western property line.\n\n**2. Overhead electric utility lines shown and their routing:**\nOverhead electric lines are visually represented on the plan by a specific line type containing the text \"OHE\".\n*   **South Boundary Route**: A utility line labeled specifically as \"**— OHE —**\" runs parallel to and just outside or along the entire southern property boundary line from west to east.\n*   **East Boundary Route**: A similarly labeled line \"**— OHE —**\" runs north-to-south along or just outside the eastern property boundary. \n*   These two \"OHE\" lines appear to meet/intersect near the southeast corner of the property. No overhead electric lines are shown routing directly through the interior of the site or over the proposed buildings.\n\n**3. Location of utility poles or overhead infrastructure:**\n*   Near the northwest corner of the site boundary (off-site, near the driveway entrance to the public road), there are distinct labels pointing to infrastructure: \"**Existing Utility Pole**\" and \"**AT&T Pole**\".\n*   Along the identified \"— OHE —\" lines on the south and east boundaries, there are standard circle symbols periodically placed at vertices or intersections that typically denote utility poles in civil drafting, though they do not have explicit text labels saying \"Pole\" next to them along those specific south/east runs.\n\n**4. Retaining walls and their locations:**\nExtensive retaining walls are proposed near the property perimeter, often situated between the buildings/driveways and the property boundary (and consequently, the OHE lines). They are explicitly labeled on the plan:\n*   **North/East Perimeter**: A long retaining wall curves around the detention pond at the north. Labels include \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall**\", \"**Concrete Retaining Wall**\", and \"**End Concrete Retaining Wall**\". This wall continues south down the eastern boundary.\n*   **East Perimeter**: Near Bldg. 5 and Bldg. 6, there is a note indicating \"**Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced**\".\n*   **South Perimeter**: A wall runs along the southern boundary parallel to Bldg. 7, Bldg. 8, and the south OHE line. Labels indicate \"**Begin Concrete Retaining Wall**\", \"**Concrete Retaining Wall**\", \"**End Concrete Retaining Wall Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall**\", and \"**Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall**\".\n\n**5. Driveways and parking areas relative to overhead lines:**\n*   The primary internal driveway enters from the west, splits, and forms a loop around the site's interior. \n*   The southern leg of this internal driveway runs east-west, parallel to Bldg. 7, Bldg. 8, the southern retaining wall, and the southern \"— OHE —\" line. \n*   The eastern leg of the driveway runs parallel to Bldg. 5, Bldg. 6, the eastern retaining wall, and the eastern \"— OHE —\" line.\n*   Parking spaces (compact and standard) are positioned along these driveways. Because the OHE lines are located on the extreme outer perimeter of the property boundaries, the driveways and parking areas do not appear to be directly underneath the OHE lines, but they are adjacent to them, separated by the property setbacks, landscape buffer areas, and retaining walls.\n\n**6. Building overhangs, awnings, or canopies extending toward overhead lines:**\n*   The building footprints feature dashed perimeter lines that typically indicate roof overhangs or eaves. \n*   While these dashed lines extend slightly outward from the solid footprint lines of Bldg. 5, 6, 7, and 8, they appear to stay well within the property boundaries and building setback limits. \n*   There is no visual evidence on this plan of any building overhangs, large awnings, or canopies physically extending over the property line or directly crossing into the path of the indicated \"— OHE —\" lines.\n\n**7. Clearance dimensions or notes related to overhead electric facilities:**\n*   A thorough review of the drawing space, dimensional arrows, and the provided text sections (including \"Site Plan Release Notes\", \"Lighting Note\", \"Trash Collection Notes\", \"Accessibility Notes\", \"Legal Description\", and the \"Texas 811 Call Before You Dig!!\" box) yields **no explicit clearance dimensions or specific warning notes** regarding vertical or horizontal clearance distances required from the overhead electric facilities to the proposed structures.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1458,"outputTokens":1262,"totalTokens":6132,"reasoningTokens":3412},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the site plan and identify all proposed buildings, structures, and site features relative to any shown overhead electric facilities. Please describe: 1) the locations of all 8 buildings (Buildings 1-8) and their proximity to property boundaries, 2) any overhead electric utility lines shown on this plan and their routing, 3) the location of utility poles or overhead infrastructure, 4) retaining walls and their locations, 5) driveways and parking areas relative to any overhead lines, 6) whether any building overhangs, awnings, or canopies are shown extending toward overhead lines, 7) any clearance dimensions or notes related to overhead electric facilities. Use the main drawing area to identify features."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-HSwBye432Nj6psCaqeX62nbZ","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 17 Apr 2026 20:41:56 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-stat