{"level":30,"time":1776460000011,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ph28sU9yUWpT4nAjcZmHHJ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a meticulous visual analysis of the provided document (Sheet 29 of 35, titled \"TREE LIST\"), here is the information regarding your specific requests. \n\nPlease note that this particular page consists solely of a **\"SURVEYED TREES\"** table, which catalogs *existing* trees on the site, their condition, whether they are to remain or be removed, and the subsequent mitigation *requirements*. It does not contain a planting schedule or site map.\n\n**1. A complete list of all proposed mitigation trees to be planted (indicated by \"M\" designation)**\nThere are no proposed mitigation trees to be planted (no \"M\" designations) listed on this document. The \"TREE NO.\" column lists numerical identifiers for existing surveyed trees (e.g., \"143\", \"4001\", \"4030a\"), but none are designated with an \"M\" for new plantings.\n\n**2. For each mitigation tree, note its species/type, caliper size (diameter in inches), and location on the site plan**\nThis information is not present on this sheet. Because this sheet only lists existing surveyed trees and does not include a site plan map, no locations, species, or caliper sizes for *proposed* mitigation plantings are available here. \n\n**3. Identify which mitigation trees are proposed near or under the overhead electric line on the southern boundary of the site**\nThis cannot be determined from this document. There is no site plan, map, or spatial data on this sheet to indicate tree locations relative to boundaries or overhead electric lines.\n\n**4. Note whether the tree species are listed in the ECM Appendix F \"Utility Compatible\" category (look for \"UC\" designation or similar notation)**\nThere is no \"UC\" or \"Utility Compatible\" designation present in this table. \nThe table does include a column titled **\"APPENDIX F (Y/N) OR INVASIVE (I)\"** which evaluates the *existing* surveyed trees. Under this column, trees are marked strictly with:\n*   **\"Y\"** (e.g., Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Pecan)\n*   **\"N\"** (e.g., Arizona Ash, Pine, Bradford Pear)\n*   **\"I\"** (e.g., China Berry)\n\n**5. Describe any clearance annotations or notes related to trees near overhead facilities**\nThere are no clearance annotations or notes regarding overhead facilities on this page. The only note provided on this sheet is located at the bottom left:\n`* TREE SURVEY PROVIDED BY SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC. SURVEY DATE: 03/28/2023`\n\n*Note: As this is only a single page (Sheet 29) of the primary site plan, the proposed mitigation planting schedule, site plan map showing utility lines, and specific \"UC\" designations are likely located on different sheets (such as a Landscape Plan or Mitigation Plan).*"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1a6fb5a-883d-4cd9-82be-985a56b0d602","uuid":"749cbe66-b67e-40bf-8960-220d9c8dbcd4","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a meticulous visual analysis of the provided document (Sheet 29 of 35, titled \"TREE LIST\"), here is the information regarding your specific requests. \n\nPlease note that this particular page consists solely of a **\"SURVEYED TREES\"** table, which catalogs *existing* trees on the site, their condition, whether they are to remain or be removed, and the subsequent mitigation *requirements*. It does not contain a planting schedule or site map.\n\n**1. A complete list of all proposed mitigation trees to be planted (indicated by \"M\" designation)**\nThere are no proposed mitigation trees to be planted (no \"M\" designations) listed on this document. The \"TREE NO.\" column lists numerical identifiers for existing surveyed trees (e.g., \"143\", \"4001\", \"4030a\"), but none are designated with an \"M\" for new plantings.\n\n**2. For each mitigation tree, note its species/type, caliper size (diameter in inches), and location on the site plan**\nThis information is not present on this sheet. Because this sheet only lists existing surveyed trees and does not include a site plan map, no locations, species, or caliper sizes for *proposed* mitigation plantings are available here. \n\n**3. Identify which mitigation trees are proposed near or under the overhead electric line on the southern boundary of the site**\nThis cannot be determined from this document. There is no site plan, map, or spatial data on this sheet to indicate tree locations relative to boundaries or overhead electric lines.\n\n**4. Note whether the tree species are listed in the ECM Appendix F \"Utility Compatible\" category (look for \"UC\" designation or similar notation)**\nThere is no \"UC\" or \"Utility Compatible\" designation present in this table. \nThe table does include a column titled **\"APPENDIX F (Y/N) OR INVASIVE (I)\"** which evaluates the *existing* surveyed trees. Under this column, trees are marked strictly with:\n*   **\"Y\"** (e.g., Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Pecan)\n*   **\"N\"** (e.g., Arizona Ash, Pine, Bradford Pear)\n*   **\"I\"** (e.g., China Berry)\n\n**5. Describe any clearance annotations or notes related to trees near overhead facilities**\nThere are no clearance annotations or notes regarding overhead facilities on this page. The only note provided on this sheet is located at the bottom left:\n`* TREE SURVEY PROVIDED BY SINCLAIR LAND SURVEYING, INC. SURVEY DATE: 03/28/2023`\n\n*Note: As this is only a single page (Sheet 29) of the primary site plan, the proposed mitigation planting schedule, site plan map showing utility lines, and specific \"UC\" designations are likely located on different sheets (such as a Landscape Plan or Mitigation Plan).*"}]}
