{"level":30,"time":1776460015036,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Yd2FBT5FJoKvof7Y5E1Ua","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 35 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: notes — Notes related to tree preservation calculations.\n     4→\n     5→NOTES:\n     6→1. CHINABERRY AND BRADFORD PEAR ARE INVASIVE TREES AND REQUIRE NO MITIGATION.\n     7→2. ASH TREES REQUIRE NO MITIGATION DUE TO EMERALD ASH BORER.\n     8→\n     9→## Block 3: notes — Notes on special construction techniques.\n    10→\n    11→SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION TECHNIQUES\n    12→ECM 3.5.4 (D)\n    13→1. PRIOR TO EXCAVATION WITHIN TREE DRIP LINES OR THE REMOVAL OF\n    14→TREES ADJACENT TO OTHER TREES THAT ARE TO REMAIN, MAKE A\n    15→CLEAN CUT BETWEEN THE DISTURBED AND UNDISTURBED ROOT ZONES\n    16→WITH A ROCK SAW OR SIMILAR EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    17→2. IN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS THAT CANNOT BE PROTECTED DURING\n    18→CONSTRUCTION WITH FENCING AND WHERE HEAVY VEHICULAR TRAFFIC\n    19→IS ANTICIPATED, COVER THOSE AREAS WITH A MINIMUM OF 12 INCHES OF\n    20→ORGANIC MULCH TO MINIMIZE SOIL COMPACTION. IN AREAS WITH HIGH\n    21→SOIL PLASTICITY GEOTEXTILE FABRIC, PER STANDARD SPECIFICATION\n    22→620S, SHOULD BE PLACED UNDER THE MULCH TO PREVENT EXCESSIVE\n    23→MIXING OF THE SOIL AND MULCH. ADDITIONALLY, MATERIAL SUCH AS\n    24→PLYWOOD AND METAL SHEETS, COULD BE REQUIRED BY THE CITY\n    25→ARBORIST TO MINIMIZE ROOT IMPACTS FROM HEAVY EQUIPMENT.\n    26→3. ONCE THE PROJECT IS COMPLETED, ALL MATERIALS SHOULD BE\n    27→REMOVED, AND THE MULCH SHOULD BE REDUCED TO A DEPTH OF 3\n    28→INCHES. PERFORM ALL GRADING WITHIN CRITICAL ROOT ZONE AREAS BY\n    29→HAND OR WITH SMALL EQUIPMENT TO MINIMIZE ROOT DAMAGE.\n    30→4. WATER ALL TREES MOST HEAVILY IMPACTED BY CONSTRUCTION\n    31→ACTIVITIES DEEPLY ONCE A WEEK DURING ACCUMULATION OF THE\n    32→LEAVES.\n    33→5. WHEN INSTALLING CONCRETE ADJACENT TO THE ROOT ZONE OF A TREE,\n    34→USE A PLASTIC VAPOR BARRIER BEHIND THE CONCRETE TO PROHIBIT\n    35→LEACHING OF LIME INTO THE SOIL.\n    36→\n    37→## Block 5: notes — Plant list section heading.\n    38→\n    39→PLANT LIST\n    40→\n    41→## Block 6: notes — Notes related to the plant list.\n    42→\n    43→NOTES:\n    44→1. THE CONTRACTORS (GENERAL AND SUBCONTRACTORS) SHALL PROVIDE UNIT COSTS FOR ALL\n    45→SOFTSCAPE AND HARDSCAPE MATERIAL SPECIFIED ON THE DRAWINGS AND SPECIFICATIONS. UNIT\n    46→COSTS SHALL BE PROVIDED FOR MATERIALS AND INSTALLATION SEPARATELY. UNIT COSTS SHALL\n    47→BE: 'EACH' FOR PLANT MATERIAL, 'SQUARE FOOT' OR 'SQUARE YARD' FOR PAVEMENTS, LINEAR FOOT\n    48→FOR WALL AND FENCE, 'EACH' FOR SITE FURNISHINGS AND SITE AMENITIES, 'CUBIC YARD' OR 'CUBIC\n    49→FOOT' FOR SOIL, MULCH AND OTHER BULK PRODUCTS AND 'EACH' OR 'LUMP SUM' FOR\n    50→MISCELLANEOUS ITEMS. THE UNIT COST SHALL BE FORMATTED TO HAVE COLUMNS FOR; ITEMS, UNIT,\n    51→UNIT COST, TOTAL ITEM COST.\n    52→2. PLANT QUANTITIES ARE PROVIDED FOR OWNER CONVENIENCE ONLY. CONTRACTOR IS\n    53→RESPONSIBLE FOR VERIFYING AND PROVIDING PLANT QUANTITIES SHOWN ON THE LANDSCAPE PLAN.\n    54→3. CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR LOCATING AND SECURING TREE AND PLANT MATERIAL IN\n    55→ADVANCE. BECAUSE OF THE LONG LEAD TIME ON THIS INSTALLATION AND THE RECENT SHORTAGE\n    56→ON TREE CROP, CONTRACTOR SHALL RESERVE OR CONTRACT GROW TREES WITH A GROWER.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 11: table — Header for City of Austin Tree Preservation Calculations.\n    59→\n    60→CITY OF AUSTIN\n    61→TREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS:\n    62→\n    63→## Block 12: table — Calculations related to tree preservation.\n    64→\n    65→EXISTING TREES:\n    66→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 212 INCHES\n    67→(HERITAGE)\n    68→24 INCHES AND GREATER, ECM APP. F TREES 0 INCHES\n    69→(NON HERITAGE)\n    70→19 TO 23.9 INCHES, ECM APP. F TREES 