{"level":30,"time":1776460059633,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01QAMYUUKZoaYWpzRyt73JKi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see that Sheet 31 has notes about landscape requirements (Block 4), but they're all related to parking lot islands, drought variance, and supplemental irrigation - nothing about tree clearances from electric facilities.\n\nThe Key Notes (Block 5) define the symbols for landscape areas (H.1-H.7) and tree abbreviations (SY, PL, P, M) but do NOT identify the SPECIES of the trees. This is the critical issue for EL-2.10.\n\nLet me now evaluate all 15 checklist items based on my findings:\n\n## SUMMARY OF FINDINGS:\n\n**CLEAR VIOLATIONS / FAILS:**\n\n1. **EL-2.10** - FAIL: Plant legend or plant schedule does not identify species of trees proposed near electric facilities\n   - Sheet 31 shows trees with symbols (SY, PL, P, M) but does not include a plant schedule identifying species\n   - Species are only identified on Sheet 35, a separate calculations sheet\n   - Trees are shown in relation to overhead electric line (OHE), but the species are not identifiable from the landscape plan itself\n\n2. **EL-2.1 or EL-2.3 or EL-2.15** - LIKELY FAIL: Trees near overhead electric line at 0 feet\n   - Measurements show trees at 0 feet lateral distance from OHE line (southern boundary)\n   - If non-utility-compatible: violates EL-2.1\n   - If large trees (40+ ft): violates EL-2.3\n   - If any tree in restricted zone without Austin Energy approval: violates EL-2.15\n   - However, due to uncertainty about exact species and utility compatibility, this might be better classified as EL-2.1 if species cannot be verified as utility-compatible\n\n**ADDITIONAL POTENTIAL ISSUES:**\n\n3. **EL-2.11** - LIKELY FAIL: Large trees not differentiated on plans to allow verification\n   - The landscape plan uses generic symbols (M, SY, PL) without distinguishing mature height categories, so large trees cannot be identified separately from smaller ones\n   - This prevents verification of whether clearances are maintained for trees that will reach 40+ feet at maturity\n\n4. **EL-2.14** - PASS: Trees shown in relation to overhead electric facilities\n   - Trees ARE shown on landscape plan\n   - Overhead electric line IS shown on landscape plan\n   - Positions appear relative to each other\n\n5. **EL-2.12, EL-2.13** - NOT APPLICABLE: No clearance dimensions shown on plans. The landscape plan does not dimension any clearances, and these items only apply if clearances ARE dimensioned.\n\nFor the remaining items, I need to verify several things: transmission facilities and easements don't appear to be identified (EL-2.2, EL-2.4, EL-2.5). I should check distances from utility poles and pad-mounted transformers. The west boundary trees at 72.9 and 96.3 feet appear to pass EL-2.8, but other areas need review. Trees within 20 feet of underground equipment need identification with root barriers verified. I also need to confirm whether Austin Energy approval was obtained for any trees at the overhead electric line setback.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3479,"cache_read_input_tokens":63413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3479},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e54b4ec-2280-4055-b825-43898abbf7bc","uuid":"b95429f5-61db-44d7-b056-5c178bd65a57"}
