{"level":30,"time":1776460264427,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HNX6ksb6qyAsXEPK9GFWhp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The plat is a historical document from 1975 (Mecey Subdivision). It would show dedicated easements but may not show voltage information for the electric lines. Let me review what I know and compile my findings:\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY - What I Found & What's Missing:**\n\n**FOUND:**\n1. ✓ Overhead electric line (OHE) along southern boundary of site\n2. ✓ Six mitigation trees planted along this OHE line\n3. ✓ Measured distances: 3 trees at 0 feet, 1 tree at 12.6 feet from conductor\n4. ✓ Electric poles on the line (trees are far from poles - >100 feet)\n5. ✓ Plant schedule with species: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud\n6. ✓ Total 20 trees proposed with 55 inches mitigation credit\n7. ✓ Austin Energy review completed (reference to UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 and Appendix F)\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n1. ✗ Whether the overhead line is distribution or transmission voltage\n2. ✗ Voltage specification (distribution < 60kV vs transmission ≥ 60kV)\n3. ✗ Utility-compatible designation for any of the proposed species\n4. ✗ Mature height specifications from ECM Appendix F for all species\n5. ✗ Austin Energy written approval for trees within clearance zones\n6. ✗ Any annotation on plans indicating electrical clearance requirements\n7. ✗ Identification of which specific species are planted in the southern row trees\n8. ✗ Large tree (40+ foot) designations noted on plans\n9. ✗ Root barrier specifications for trees near underground equipment\n10. ✗ Underground electric equipment locations and proximity to trees\n\n\n11. ✗ Specific clearance zone requirements based on voltage class\n\nNow I need to assess each checklist item against what's documented and what's missing. Several items will likely fail or be unverifiable due to absent voltage data and incomplete species specifications for the southern row.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1922,"cache_read_input_tokens":70696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1922},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"7e49d5b6-6c17-4e14-8e7c-3626fe8e8c7d"}
{"level":30,"time":1776460264427,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HNX6ksb6qyAsXEPK9GFWhp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have comprehensive information to evaluate the checklist items. Let me compile my research findings and work through each item systematically:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY - TREES & ELECTRIC CLEARANCES\n\n### FOUND:\n✓ Overhead Electric Line (OHE) along southern site boundary  \n✓ Six mitigation trees planted directly along/under OHE line  \n✓ Tree measurements: 3 trees @ 0 feet, 1 tree @ 12.6 feet from conductor  \n✓ Poles are >100 feet from trees  \n✓ Plant species proposed: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud  \n✓ Total 20 trees with 55 inches mitigation credit  \n✓ Austin Energy design criteria references UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4\n\n### NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:\n✗ Line voltage classification (distribution vs. transmission)  \n✗ Utility-compatible (UC) designation for any tree species on plans  \n✗ ECM Appendix F mature height specs cited on plans  \n✗ Austin Energy written approval for trees within clearance zones  \n✗ Electrical clearance requirements mentioned on landscape/site plans  \n✗ Specific species identification for trees in southern row (0 feet from line)  \n✗ Large tree (40+ feet) designations on plans  \n✗ Underground utility equipment locations/distances  \n✗ Root barrier specifications for any trees  \n\nNow let me evaluate each of the 15 checklist items:\n\n### CHECKLIST ITEM EVALUATIONS\n\n**EL-2.1: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution conductor**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE** \n- **Reason**: While overhead electric distribution appears to be present, the plans do NOT identify which tree species are utility-compatible. No reference to ECM Appendix F UC designation. Trees at 0 feet from line, but cannot verify species or UC status from plan documents.\n\n**EL-2.2: Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission conductor**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: Cannot determine line voltage (distribution vs. transmission) from available documents. No ECM Appendix F references or UC designations on plans. No voltage labeling on electrical design.\n\n**EL-2.3: Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution conductor**\n- **Status**: **FAIL**\n- **Reason**: Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) has 50-foot mature height per horticultural standards, qualifying as large tree (>40 ft). Three of six mitigation trees measured at 0 feet from overhead conductor (within 25-foot restriction). Live Oak appears to be included in southern boundary tree row but specific identification not verified on plan. Plant schedule does not identify large tree status or note electrical clearance restrictions for Live Oak.\n\n**EL-2.4: Large trees (40+ ft) within 50 ft of transmission conductor**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: Cannot determine line voltage from documents. If transmission line, same 50-foot applies and would fail. However, voltage not specified.\n\n**EL-2.5: Trees within transmission easement boundaries**\n- **Status**: **NOT-APPLICABLE**\n- **Reason**: No transmission easement identified in facts.md or on plat. Only distribution electric easements noted (5' easements from Mecey Subdivision).\n\n**EL-2.6: Trees within 10 ft of electric utility pole**\n- **Status**: **PASS**\n- **Reason**: Measured distances from trees to nearest electric poles: 124-321 feet. All exceed 10-foot minimum clearance from poles.\n\n**EL-2.7: Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: Sheet 21 shows underground electrical infrastructure (transformers, pull boxes) but no clear marking of pad-mounted (aboveground) equipment. Cannot verify if any trees are within 10 feet of pad-mounts.\n\n**EL-2.8: Trees within 5 ft of underground electric equipment**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: Sheet 21 shows underground electric lines and pull boxes but their exact locations not clearly dimensioned relative to tree planting areas on landscape plan. Cannot verify specific distances from proposed trees to underground equipment.\n\n**EL-2.9: Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment lack root barriers**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: No root barrier specifications appear on landscape plan details or notes. Tree locations relative to underground equipment not clearly dimensioned. Cannot verify which trees, if any, are within 20 feet of underground equipment.\n\n**EL-2.10: Plant legend/schedule does not identify tree species near electric facilities**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: While a plant schedule exists on Sheet 35 with common and scientific names, it is NOT cross-referenced on the landscape plan (Sheet 31) to show which specific trees are at which locations. The six southern-boundary trees (directly under OHE line) are not labeled with species designations on the landscape plan itself.\n\n**EL-2.11: Large trees not differentiated on plans**\n- **Status**: **FAIL**\n- **Reason**: Plant schedule lists Live Oak mature height as container-grown (no mature height specified). No notation on landscape plan indicating which trees are \"large\" (40+ feet). No differentiation of large trees in the six southern-boundary trees despite Live Oak presence (50-foot mature height).\n\n**EL-2.12: Clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: Plans do NOT show any dimensioned clearances from trees to electric lines or poles. No clearance measurements are provided on landscape or site plans, so measurement methodology cannot be evaluated.\n\n**EL-2.13: Clearances measured from canopy instead of trunk**\n- **Status**: **NOT-VERIFIABLE**\n- **Reason**: Plans do NOT show any dimensioned clearances from trees to electric infrastructure. Without dimensioned measurements on plans, measurement reference point cannot be evaluated.\n\n**EL-2.14: Trees not shown relative to overhead electric facilities**\n- **Status**: **FAIL**\n- **Reason**: While trees and OHE line are shown on landscape plan Sheet 31, the relationship is not clearly documented. The six trees planted directly under the OHE line are NOT labeled with species, clearance distances, or electrical requirement notations. No callouts or detail sheets explain the clearance compliance. Overhead line position is shown but no clearance verification provided.\n\n**EL-2.15: Trees proposed within prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval**\n- **Status**: **FAIL**\n- **Reason**: Multiple trees measured at 0 feet lateral distance from overhead electric conductor. Plans contain NO documented Austin Energy written approval authorizing trees within restricted clearance zones. No approval letters, coordination notes, or variance documentation included in site plan or supplementary documents reviewed.\n\n---\n\nNow let me prepare the structured output with findings for all items marked FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1922,"cache_read_input_tokens":70696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1922},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9937603-308a-417f-be5d-ed14424eb758","uuid":"4f0e5985-6c23-4ea3-bc38-66bbd21e3ae9"}
