{"level":30,"time":1776460264430,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DndB5zXqH5SEKF7jdQrUAq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the comprehensive site plan review for grouping EL-MD-EXP 13 (Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements).\n\n## Summary of Evaluation\n\nI evaluated all **39 checklist items** in this grouping by conducting systematic research across the site plan documents. Here are the results:\n\n**Findings Summary:**\n- **3 items marked as FAIL** (critical missing requirements)\n- **36 items marked as NOT-VERIFIABLE** (insufficient evidence on plans)\n- **0 items marked as PASS** (no deficiencies identified)\n- **0 items marked as N/A** (grouping is fully applicable to this project)\n\n### Critical Findings - FAIL Items:\n\n1. **EL-13.31 (Cross-Section Drawings)** — No cross-section drawings provided showing vertical clearances for transformer access paths, overhead structures, or parking areas. This is a direct deficiency - the required documentation is entirely missing.\n\n2. **EL-13.37 (Transformer Pad Details)** — No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are attached. No pad dimensions, kVA ratings, voltage, or service type (single-phase vs. three-phase) specifications are provided. Required AE Design details are missing.\n\n3. **EL-13.38 (Bollards for Parking Proximity)** — All 5 transformer pads are located within 4 feet of parking areas, drive aisles, or vehicle circulation routes. No 4-inch diameter galvanized rigid metal bollard details, specifications, or placement drawings are shown. Required bollards are not documented.\n\n### NOT-VERIFIABLE Items (36 total):\n\nThe remaining 36 items cannot be verified because critical supporting documentation is systematically missing from the site plans:\n\n- **No clearance dimensions** between transformer pads and buildings, fences, utilities, sidewalks, or other site features\n- **No transformer specifications** (oil-filled vs. dry-type, electrical characteristics)\n- **No access door orientation** indicators on transformer pads\n- **No utility coordination analysis** showing clearances from water, wastewater, storm drain, and gas lines\n- **No landscape species verification** for utility-compatible trees (ECM Appendix F)\n- **No root barrier specifications** for trees within 20 feet\n- **No transformer easements** shown on plat or documented\n- **No Austin Energy Design approval** documents or written approvals for any clearance reductions\n- **No electrical routing confirmation** that service is 100% on private property\n- **No fire hydrant clearance documentation**\n- **No drainage analysis** for oil-filled equipment around transformer pads\n\nThe structured output has been provided with all findings and is ready for applicant response."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9561,"cache_read_input_tokens":66110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9561},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ac40e46-c33f-4252-a569-366ec49df9f2","uuid":"e35c79be-6231-404c-bb0e-a3768062394e"}
