"Transformer pad locations if in niche configuration (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided analyzing whether any transformer is located in a niche (accessible from outside but within building footprint). No 35-foot vertical clearance documentation is provided for any niche scenarios. Compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.30","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 3"],"applicableAreas":["Transformer pads if in niche service configuration (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No niche service configurations are evident from available plans. If niche service were proposed, the required architectural specifications (3-hour fire wall rating, ventilation specifications) and Austin Energy Design coordination documentation are not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (survey requirement as required by AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations with overhead structures, parking areas, or enclosed access paths (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No cross-section drawings are provided showing vertical clearances for transformer access paths, overhead structures, parking areas, or enclosed areas. Cross-sections required to demonstrate compliance with vertical clearance requirements are missing from the site plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pads if oil-filled equipment is proposed (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer equipment specifications indicate whether equipment is oil-filled or dry-type. Grading Plan (Sheet 11) shows general site drainage flowing away from buildings, but specific surface flow direction around individual transformer pads is not documented. Drainage compliance for oil-filled equipment cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.33","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pads (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat (Sheet 2) and Site Plan (Sheet 9) show property boundaries but no explicit documentation confirms that all transformer pads are located 100% on private property and do not straddle property lines. Status cannot be verified without detailed boundary analysis."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.34","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4 (property requirement); easement-specific regulations"],"applicableAreas":["All transformer pad locations relative to drainage, water, sewer, and overhead easements (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Plat (Sheet 2) shows various easements (drainage, water, sewer, electric, public utility). Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer locations but does not clearly coordinate pad placement relative to prohibited easements. No Austin Energy Design written approval is provided if pads are located within easements. Compliance status cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3 (additional clearance and access easements may be required)"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pads (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No transformer easements are shown on the Plat (Sheet 2) or Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) surrounding the transformer pads. No easement widths or accessibility requirements are documented. Transformer easement requirements cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["Electrical routing from all transformer pads to meters (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) shows transformer locations and general electrical routing but does not explicitly confirm that the entire electrical path from transformer to meter is 100% on private property. Routing details are insufficient to verify full private property compliance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0 (obtain transformer pad detail from AE Design)"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pads (Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are referenced or attached to the site plan. Pad dimensions are not specified, and no transformer specifications (kVA, service type: single-phase or three-phase) are documented on the Electrical Plan. Compliance cannot be verified without AE Design-approved details."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.38","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["All five transformer pads adjacent to parking areas and vehicle circulation (Pads 1-5 on Sheet 21)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"All five transformer pads shown on Electrical Plan (Sheet 21) are located within 4 feet of parking areas, drive aisles, or vehicle circulation routes. No 4-inch minimum diameter galvanized rigid metal bollard specifications, spacing details, or placement drawings are provided. Required bollards are not documented."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.39","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["Customer facilities relative to overhead distribution facilities (Sheet 21, Sheet 9)"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution facilities are shown on Electrical Plan (Sheet 21). However, no cross-reference coordination is provided verifying that no customer facilities (buildings, parking garages, light poles, signs) are installed under or over Austin Energy overhead distribution lines."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"4d787a6b-57d8-4d81-8f8d-6aa227d2fbc9"}
