{"level":30,"time":1776460264431,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":35,"prompt":"Examine the plant list schedules on this landscape calculations sheet. Specifically:\n1. Provide a complete list of all shade trees to be planted, including species names, quantities, and container sizes\n2. List all ornamental trees with species and quantities\n3. Note whether any of these trees are identified as \"Utility Compatible\" (UC) per ECM Appendix F\n4. Cross-reference the tree species listed against the legend definition of mature height (note that UC trees are typically ≤20 feet mature height)\n5. Identify which tree species would be appropriate for planting near overhead distribution conductors (within 10 feet lateral distance per ECM § 2.4.1.D)\n\nAlso check if there's any note or reference to overhead electric clearance requirements in the plant schedule instructions.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the \"PLANT LIST\" schedule and notes provided on the landscape calculations sheet, here is the analysis:\n\n**1. Shade Trees to be Planted (Species, Quantities, Container Sizes)**\n*   **Live Oak** (*Quercus virginiana*): Quantity 2, Container Size: 100 GAL. (Min. Spec: \"100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN\")\n*   **Cedar Elm** (*Ulmus crassifolia*): Quantity 10, Container Size: 100 GAL. (Min. Spec: \"100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN\")\n*(Note: An \"Existing Tree, to be preserved\" is also listed under shade trees with no quantity or container size).*\n\n**2. Ornamental Trees (Species and Quantities)**\n*   **Texas Mountain Laurel** (*Sophora secundiflora*): Quantity 2\n*   **Mexican Redbud** (*Cercis canadensis var. mexicana*): Quantity 6\n\n**3. \"Utility Compatible\" (UC) Identification**\nNone of the trees listed in the schedule are explicitly marked, tagged, or identified with \"Utility Compatible\" or \"UC\". \n\n**4 & 5. Mature Height Cross-Reference & Suitability Near Overhead Conductors**\nThere is no legend or definition for *mature* heights included on this specific document sheet (only *minimum planting heights* of 8', 10', and 16' are provided). However, based on standard botanical characteristics for the species listed:\n*   **Appropriate for planting near overhead conductors (≤20 feet mature height):** The listed Ornamental Trees (**Texas Mountain Laurel** and **Mexican Redbud**) are small, understory trees that generally mature at or below 20 feet. These would typically be the appropriate selections for planting within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors.\n*   **Inappropriate for planting near overhead conductors:** The listed Shade Trees (**Live Oak** and **Cedar Elm**) are large canopy trees that mature well over 20 feet in height. They would *not* be appropriate for planting near overhead distribution lines. \n\n**Notes or References to Overhead Electric Clearance**\nA careful review of all note sections on this sheet (including the \"PLANT LIST\" Notes, \"CITY OF AUSTIN LANDSCAPE CALCULATIONS\" Notes, and \"SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT LANDSCAPE\" Notes) reveals **no references** to overhead electric clearance requirements, utility lines, or utility compatibility.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1472,"outputTokens":536,"totalTokens":4117,"reasoningTokens":2109},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2584864]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the plant list schedules on this landscape calculations sheet. Specifically:\n1. Provide a complete list of all shade trees to be planted, including species names, quantities, and container sizes\n2. List all ornamental trees with species and quantities\n3. Note whether any of these trees are identified as \"Utility Compatible\" (UC) per ECM Appendix F\n4. Cross-reference the tree species listed against the legend definition of mature height (note that UC trees are typically ≤20 feet mature height)\n5. Identify which tree species would be appropriate for planting near overhead distribution conductors (within 10 feet lateral distance per ECM § 2.4.1.D)\n\nAlso check if there's any note or reference to overhead electric clearance requirements in the plant schedule instructions."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-uCCzAtqbFwO5Gncte0gYMu8f","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language