 conductors:** The listed Shade Trees (**Live Oak** and **Cedar Elm**) are large canopy trees that mature well over 20 feet in height. They would *not* be appropriate for planting near overhead distribution lines. \n\n**Notes or References to Overhead Electric Clearance**\nA careful review of all note sections on this sheet (including the \"PLANT LIST\" Notes, \"CITY OF AUSTIN LANDSCAPE CALCULATIONS\" Notes, and \"SITE DEVELOPMENT PERMIT LANDSCAPE\" Notes) reveals **no references** to overhead electric clearance requirements, utility lines, or utility compatibility."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1a6fb5a-883d-4cd9-82be-985a56b0d602","uuid":"ef4482b2-ff58-463d-9d8a-3b0250f1d5df","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the \"PLANT LIST\" schedule and notes provided on the landscape calculations sheet, here is the analysis:\n\n**1. Shade Trees to be Planted (Species, Quantities, Container Sizes)**\n*   **Live Oak** (*Quercus virginiana*): Quantity 2, Container Size: 100 GAL. (Min. Spec: \"100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN\")\n*   **Cedar Elm** (*Ulmus crassifolia*): Quantity 10, Container Size: 100 GAL. (Min. Spec: \"100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM CONTAINER GROWN\")\n*(Note: An \"Existing Tree, to be preserved\" is also listed under shade trees with no quantity or container size).*\n\n**2. Ornamental Trees (Species and Quantities)**\n*   **Texas Mountain Laurel** (*Sophora secundiflora*): Quantity 2\n*   **Mexican Redbud** (*Cercis canadensis var. mexicana*): Quantity 6\n\n**3. \"Utility Compatible\" (UC) Identification**\nNone of the trees listed in the schedule are explicitly marked, tagged, or identified with \"Utility Compatible\" or \"UC\". \n\n**4 & 5. Mature Height Cross-Reference & Suitability Near Overhead Conductors**\nThere is no legend or definition for *mature* heights included on this specific document sheet (only *minimum planting heights* of 8', 10', and 16' are provided). However, based on standard bota