{"level":30,"time":1776460287565,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":38,"prompt":"Please examine this retaining wall plan and tell me:\n\n1. Are the existing overhead utility lines (OHE) or any overhead electric infrastructure shown on this plan view?\n\n2. What is the location and extent of the retaining walls relative to the property boundaries (specifically relative to Valley View Road where the overhead lines are)?\n\n3. Are there any dimension lines or clearance annotations showing distances from the retaining walls to existing overhead electric lines or poles?\n\n4. Are there any section views shown that indicate vertical clearances between the walls and any overhead utilities?\n\n5. Do any of the wall sections or details show clearance considerations from overhead facilities?\n\nPlease describe the specific locations of walls and any nearby utilities noted.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided retaining wall plan document (Sheet 38 of 39 for the project located at \"3759 VALLEY VIEW\"), here are the answers to your specific questions:\n\n**1. Are the existing overhead utility lines (OHE) or any overhead electric infrastructure shown on this plan view?**\nNo. There are no overhead utility lines (OHE), utility poles, or any overhead electric infrastructure visually depicted anywhere in the \"PLAN VIEW\" or anywhere else on this sheet.\n\n**2. What is the location and extent of the retaining walls relative to the property boundaries (specifically relative to Valley View Road where the overhead lines are)?**\nIt is not possible to determine this from the provided document. The \"PLAN VIEW\" shows localized geometry of the walls (labeled \"POND WALL\", \"EXISTING WALL\", and \"NEW RETAINING WALL\"), but it does not contain any property lines, right-of-way (ROW) lines, or street names (such as Valley View Road). The only geographical reference on the page is in the title block, which reads \"3759 VALLEY VIEW\".\n\n**3. Are there any dimension lines or clearance annotations showing distances from the retaining walls to existing overhead electric lines or poles?**\nNo. There are no dimension lines or annotations indicating clearances or distances to any overhead utility infrastructure. All dimensions provided relate strictly to the structural geometry of the retaining wall itself (e.g., footing widths, wall heights, rebar spacing).\n\n**4. Are there any section views shown that indicate vertical clearances between the walls and any overhead utilities?**\nNo. The section views provided (\"14'-0\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\" and \"TYPICAL STEP IN FOOTING\") focus exclusively on the structural details, concrete reinforcement, footing depths, and backfill requirements. They do not depict the space above the wall or any overhead utilities.\n\n**5. Do any of the wall sections or details show clearance considerations from overhead facilities?**\nNo. None of the sections or details show clearance considerations for overhead facilities. The only mention of utilities on this page is a general note regarding existing lines prior to digging, found under \"NOTES\":\n> \"2. OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION.\"\n\n**Specific locations of walls and nearby utilities noted:**\n\n*   **Walls:** The \"PLAN VIEW\" shows a solid, thick-lined structure consisting of multiple segments labeled \"POND WALL REF PG 2\". Attached to this is a thick, dashed line representing the \"NEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\". Running roughly parallel to the new retaining wall is a thinner solid line labeled \"EXISTING WALL\". A specific connection point is noted: \"EXISTING BUTTRESS DRILL AND EPOXY #6 X 12\" DOWELS 6\" INTO BUTTRESS 12\" O.C. TIE TO WALL STEEL.\"\n*   **Utilities:** As stated, no specific nearby utilities (overhead or underground) are graphically located, noted, or drawn on this plan.\n\n***\n\n**Additional Document Transcriptions (per instructions for exact table reproduction):**\n\nFor completeness based on your instructions to exactly reproduce tables found on the document, here are the contents of the tables located in the lower right portion of the sheet:\n\n**REQUIRED INSPECTIONS:**\n> 1. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF FOOTINGS.\n> 2. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF WALLS.\n> 3. PRIOR TO BACKFILL PLACEMENT TO VERIFY FILTER FABRIC AND DRAINAGE GRAVEL.\n\n**DESIGN CRITERIA:**\n> REQUIREMENTS OF IBC 2015\n> *ALLOWABLE SOIL BEARING : 4,000 PSF\n> *LATERAL PRESSURE METHOD : E.F.P.\n> *ACTIVE SOIL PRESSURE - HEEL : 45.5 PSF\n> *PASSIVE PRESSURE : 250 PSF\n> *SOIL WEIGHT : 130 PSF","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1454,"outputTokens":830,"totalTokens":4042,"reasoningTokens":1758},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1208488]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine this retaining wall plan and tell me:\n\n1. Are the existing overhead utility lines (OHE) or any overhead electric infrastructure shown on this plan view?\n\n2. What is the location and extent of the retaining walls relative to the property boundaries (specifically relative to Valley View Road where the overhead lines are)?\n\n3. Are there any dimension lines or clearance annotations showing distances from the retaining walls to existing overhead electric lines or poles?\n\n4. Are there any section views shown that indicate vertical clearances between the walls and any overhead utilities?\n\n5. Do any of the wall sections or details show clearance considerations from overhead facilities?\n\nPlease describe the specific locations of walls and any nearby utilities noted."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-AJlqK3QHXLfVLMd8z6Ixj1eV","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Fri, 17 Apr 2026 21:11:27 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","tra