{"level":30,"time":1776460289730,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FeKnTDCSwAKDyK4jpc3CQx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see there are sheets all the way to 39. Based on the README:\n- Sheet 22-28: Construction Details (mostly for utility infrastructure - water, wastewater, fire, storm)\n- Sheet 37-39: Landscape Details and Wall Plans/Details\n\nNone of these appear to be building elevations that would show overhead electric clearances. The project seems to focus on site plan and utilities details rather than detailed building elevations.\n\nNow let me do a comprehensive evaluation of each checklist item based on my research findings. I'll organize by status:\n\n**APPLICABILITY CHECK:**\n- The site HAS overhead electric facilities (Sheet 4, Sheet 31)\n- The site HAS proposed buildings, driveways, parking, and landscaping\n- Therefore, clearance requirements apply\n\n**KEY RESEARCH FINDINGS:**\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Facilities Documented:**\n   - Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions): Shows utility poles and overhead lines on western and northern boundaries, with one down guy anchor on northern boundary\n   - Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan): Shows overhead electric line on southern boundary\n   - Sheet 21 (Electrical Design): Shows proposed underground infrastructure only\n\n2. **Missing Documentation:**\n   - No proximity survey showing existing Austin Energy facilities and proposed improvements\n   - No clearance dimensions shown on any site plan sheets\n   - No elevation sheets or sections showing vertical clearances\n   - No building elevation views\n\n3. **Tree Clearance Issue:**\n   - Sheet 31 shows 5 mitigation trees (\"M\") directly over/adjacent to overhead line on southern boundary\n   - Sheet 35 specifies: Cedar Elm (10x), Live Oak (2x), Texas Mountain Laurel (2x), Mexican Redbud (6x)\n   - Cedar Elm and Live Oak mature heights exceed 20 feet (NOT utility-compatible per UCM § 1.10.10.4)\n   - No \"UC\" (Utility Compatible) designation provided\n   - No clearance verification from ECM Appendix F\n   \n4. **Missing Contractor Notification:** No plan note requiring Austin Energy notification before work near overhead lines. Additionally, a down guy anchor is visible on Sheet 4's northern boundary with no corresponding easement documentation or guy anchor easement exhibit provided.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":63988,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1787},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1a6fb5a-883d-4cd9-82be-985a56b0d602","uuid":"1eed3685-ef53-41f7-8a4d-6e08c020aab2"}
{"level":30,"time":1776460294018,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01FeKnTDCSwAKDyK4jpc3CQx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive research, I have identified the key issues. Now let me systematically evaluate each checklist item and prepare my findings.\n\n**RESEARCH SUMMARY:**\n\n**Overhead Electric Infrastructure Located:**\n- Sheet 4 (Existing Conditions Survey): Overhead utility lines and poles shown along western and northern property boundaries; one down guy anchor on northern boundary\n- Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan): Overhead electric line (\"-OHE-\") shown along southern boundary of site\n- Sheet 21 (Preliminary Electrical Design): Shows proposed underground electrical infrastructure only\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n1. **No clearance dimensions shown** - Overhead line on southern boundary (Sheet 31) crosses site with no clearance annotations to buildings, structures, or proposed trees\n2. **No building elevation/section views** - No engineered profiles showing vertical clearances from overhead conductors to building features\n3. **No proximity survey** - No survey documenting existing Austin Energy facilities and proposed site improvements\n4. **Trees near overhead facilities** - Sheet 31 shows 5 mitigation trees (\"M\") directly over/adjacent to overhead line; Sheet 35 specifies Cedar Elm (10) and Live Oak (2) which are NOT utility-compatible species for planting within 10 feet of overhead distribution lines; no \"UC\" (Utility Compatible) designation provided\n5. **No 48-hour notification note** - No plan note requiring contractor notification to Austin Energy before construction near overhead lines\n6. **Guy anchor easement missing** - Down guy anchor shown on Sheet 4 but no easement documentation or easement exhibit provided\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE ITEMS** (Evidence absent or ambiguous):\n- EL-1.1 through EL-1.8, EL-1.14, EL-1.17, EL-1.23, EL-1.31 - No clearance dimensions shown\n- EL-1.7 - No surveyed overhead conductor elevations on building elevations\n- EL-1.37 - Tree species near overhead lines not verified as utility-compatible\n- EL-1.42, EL-1.41 - Guy easement documentation missing\n- EL-1.46 - 48-hour notification note missing\n\n**FAIL ITEMS** (Deficiency is present):\n- EL-1.37 - Trees (Cedar Elm, Live Oak) proposed near overhead line do not meet utility-compatible requirement for 10-foot lateral distance\n\nLet me prepare the final structured output with only the fail and not-verifiable items:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1787,"cache_read_input_tokens":63988,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1787},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1a6fb5a-883d-4cd9-82be-985a56b0d602","uuid":"c21dca9b-24d3-48f5-8127-600af4f5eaac"}
{"level":30,"time":1776460295372,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Cs1zw9TEHCPp33BT13C8bB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! The Electric Review section mentions:\n- UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities ← This is exactly what the grouping is about\n- UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n- UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n- Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual (tree species)\n\nThere's a Bluebeam link to download Austin Energy review comments. I don't have access to that link directly, but it confirms that Austin Energy has been asked to review the project and that clearance requirements under UCM § 1.10.3 and tree requirements under Appendix F are relevant.\n\nNow let me compile my findings. Based on my research, here's what I've found:\n\n## RESEARCH SUMMARY\n\n**Existing Conditions (from Sheet 4 survey):**\n- Overhead utility lines exist along the western (Valley View Road), northern, and southern property boundaries\n- Multiple utility poles exist on or near the property\n- Electric easements are recorded: \n  - 10' ELEC. & TELE. EASEMENT on northern boundary\n  - 5' ELEC. EASEMENT on eastern boundary (VOL. 4236, PG. 78)\n  - 5' ELEC. EASEMENT on southern boundary (VOL. 5184, PG. 16)\n  - Additional easements from historical plats\n\n**Proposed Facilities:**\n- 8 townhome buildings\n- Retaining walls along eastern and southern property boundaries (near overhead electric lines and easements)\n- Driveways and parking areas near the overhead lines\n- Landscape plan shows 5 mitigation trees (marked \"M\") along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line\n- Proposed tree species: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud, and others\n\n\n- Underground electrical distribution serving the buildings per Sheet 21\n\nSeveral critical items are missing from the plans. There are no clearance dimensions shown between the buildings and overhead lines, no section or profile views demonstrating vertical or horizontal clearances, and no clearance measurements from the retaining walls to the overhead lines. The landscape plan doesn't specify which tree species are planted near the southern boundary overhead line, nor does it indicate whether those species are utility-compatible. Additionally, the cover sheet lacks the required 48-hour notification note, surveyed conductor elevations aren't shown on building elevations, and there's no documentation of clearances from driveways and parking areas to the overhead lines.\n\nThis grouping applies to the site because overhead electric facilities exist on or adjacent to the property, and the proposed buildings, structures, landscaping, and utilities are positioned within potential clearance distances. The development must maintain required clearances from these facilities.\n\nEvaluating the checklist systematically reveals several items that are clearly not applicable: no substation exists on the property, so fencing requirements for substations don't apply; transmission line fencing requirements are unclear since the easements only indicate \"electric\" without confirming transmission versus distribution lines; retaining wall-to-substation clearances don't apply without a substation; and transmission line clearance standards cannot be verified without confirmed transmission lines.\n\nAdditional items fall outside the scope or lack sufficient information: highway/freeway underbuilt distribution doesn't apply to this site; customer facilities under or over distribution lines need verification; foundation setbacks from adjacent property lines cannot be assessed without knowing if neighboring properties contain utilities; new poles for underground conversion aren't shown in the project plans; guy easements for transmission lines don't apply if transmission lines aren't present; down guy anchor easements require verification of existing down guys; niche-mounted transformers aren't depicted; construction staging falls outside the site plan review scope; and service masts through roofs aren't visible on the available elevation drawings.\n\nThe project will fail review due to missing critical clearance documentation. Buildings 5 through 8 lack any clearance dimensions to overhead lines, and no surveyed conductor elevations appear on the building elevations. Section and profile exhibits showing distances from outer conductors are absent. Retaining walls along the southern and eastern boundaries have no clearance dimensions shown, and no section exhibits demonstrate adequate clearance. Driveways and parking pads near overhead facilities lack vertical clearance verification. Without these dimensional exhibits, compliance with clearance requirements cannot be demonstrated.\n\nAdditional deficiencies include no registered surveyor data for mid-span clearances, trees within 10 lateral feet of the southern boundary OHE line that aren't on the utility-compatible species list, and missing 48-hour notification language on the plans. Several items require further clarification—radial clearance from distribution facilities depends on conductor type, elevated walkways and platforms are unclear, and vehicle barriers and emergency access structures need verification. through the checklist systematically to determine status for each item.\n\nI need to evaluate each standard against the site conditions to identify which ones apply and what their current compliance status is.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":70515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2571f496-befa-43e1-bc2b-06222dd9dc2e","uuid":"0039c923-c922-4b97-9e41-087e887dce8a"}
{"level":30,"time":1776460297832,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Cs1zw9TEHCPp33BT13C8bB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my research, I have comprehensive information about the site's electrical infrastructure and proposed development. Let me now systematically evaluate each checklist item.\n\n## RESEARCH PHASE FINDINGS\n\n**Existing Overhead Electric Facilities:**\n- Overhead utility lines (OHE) exist along Valley View Road (western boundary), northern boundary, and southern boundary\n- Multiple utility poles on/adjacent to property (northwest corner, northern midpoint, northeast corner, southwest corner)\n- Electric easements recorded on northern, eastern, and southern boundaries (5'-10' widths)\n- Guy wires present on some poles\n\n**Proposed Development Features Near Overhead Lines:**\n- Buildings 5, 6, 7, 8 located within potential clearance distance of eastern/southern boundary overhead lines\n- Retaining walls proposed along eastern and southern boundaries parallel to overhead lines\n- Internal driveways and parking areas adjacent to overhead lines\n- Landscape plan shows 5 mitigation trees (\"M\") planted along southern boundary near overhead electric line\n- Proposed tree species: Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud (all large shade trees)\n\n**CRITICAL MISSING INFORMATION:**\n- NO clearance dimensions from buildings/structures to overhead conductors\n- NO section or profile exhibits showing vertical/horizontal clearances\n- NO surveyed conductor elevations on building elevations  \n- NO specification of tree species location (cannot confirm if they're the 5 southern boundary trees)\n- NO indication of tree species utility-compatibility per ECM Appendix F\n- NO 48-hour notification note on plans\n- NO registered surveyor data for mid-span clearances\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":70515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2571f496-befa-43e1-bc2b-06222dd9dc2e","uuid":"6e1e832c-f77d-4c9d-a627-6d4302c1c804"}
{"level":30,"time":1776460297988,"pid":85817,"hostname":"Williams-MBP.lan","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01U1jDkv9aKGNVKKzfR9Tv4r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! The vision analysis shows that:\n1. NO overhead utility lines are shown on Sheet 38\n2. No clearance annotations or dimensions from retaining walls to utilities\n3. The note says \"OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION\" but no clearance specifications\n\nThis is important for EL-1.14 and EL-1.17. Let me now systematically go through the checklist and make my final determinations.\n\nGiven my research, here are the key findings:\n\n**CONFIRMED NOT-VERIFIABLE OR FAIL ITEMS:**\n\n1. **EL-1.7 - FAIL**: Surveyed elevations and locations of overhead conductors not included on building elevation sheets. No building elevation sheets provided.\n\n2. **EL-1.8 - FAIL**: Section and plan view exhibits do not show dimensions from outer conductor to building edges. No such exhibits provided.\n\n3. **EL-1.31 - FAIL**: Survey by registered surveyor showing pole locations and mid-span clearances not provided.\n\n4. **EL-1.37 - FAIL**: Trees proposed within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors appear not to have been verified as utility-compatible species. Sheet 31 shows trees within 5-10 feet of OHE line, Sheet 35 lists Live Oak and Cedar Elm, but no specification that these are utility-compatible or maintain clearances.\n\n5. **EL-1.46 - FAIL**: Plans do not include required note about 48-hour notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage overhead lines. This note is not found on Cover Sheet or General Notes.\n\n6. **EL-1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.6, 1.18, 1.23, 1.43** - **NOT-VERIFIABLE**: These all require clearance dimensions or survey data that are not provided on the plans. Without these, compliance cannot be verified.\n \nWhile the site plan shows Buildings 1 and 8 positioned 26.1' and 33.3' from Valley View Road where the overhead lines run, this distance alone doesn't establish compliance—the conductors may be offset from the road edge and have significant vertical extent. Without surveyed conductor elevations, section views showing conductor height relative to building faces, dimension lines from the outer conductor to structures, and verified mid-span clearance data, I cannot confirm that EL-1.1, 1.2, 1.3, 1.6, 1.18, 1.23, and similar items meet requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1291,"cache_read_input_tokens":70711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1291},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ebd3136-3d68-467e-99f2-1be8af4a9563","uuid":"7b1ea2f0-7b70-486f-ba5c-1f8cf5dd5c6d"}
