ranging from 683.0 to 687.50; finished driveway grades around 680-686) appear marginal relative to estimated overhead line heights. No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data are provided showing measured vertical clearances from overhead conductors to buildings, driveways, or parking areas to verify compliance with minimum required clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape plan southern property boundary where overhead electric utility line is routed and five mitigation trees are proposed"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan shows five mitigation trees (marked 'M') planted along the southern property boundary in proximity to the overhead electric utility line. The specific species of these five trees is not identified on the landscape plan or cross-referenced to the plant schedule on Sheet 35. The proposed tree species for the project (Live Oak, Cedar Elm, Texas Mountain Laurel, Mexican Redbud) are large shade trees that do not appear to be utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F standards. Cannot verify that trees within 10 lateral feet of overhead distribution conductors (or 50 lateral feet of transmission conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4) are from the Utility Compatible list."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Cover sheet and general notes where overhead electric lines exist on or adjacent to construction site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines (per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, 